2026-11-28  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	decode: check the handles page against the section before its CRC, GHSA-w67w-f2fw-prvj
	read_2004_section_handles and read_2007_section_handles computed the CRC
	of a handles page over hdl_dat.byte - secpos, and then read the 2 CRC
	bytes. A malformed object map advances the cursor past the decompressed
	section, so bit_calc_CRC read past the buffer.

	The reported PoC (from 00472304a) is already fixed by 595d06189, which
	stopped the r2004 handles resync at the end of the buffer. This is the
	second guard, for any other way the cursor leaves the section, and it
	also covers the r2007 reader, which has no such resync fix.

	Reported-by: GHSA-w67w-f2fw-prvj reporter

	* src/decode.c (read_2004_section_handles): Stop with
	  DWG_ERR_VALUEOUTOFBOUNDS when the page plus its CRC exceeds the section.
	* src/decode_r2007.c (read_2007_section_handles): Likewise.

2026-11-28  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	dxf: the LTYPE dash text must end in its strings_area, GHSA-37w4-c8mv-7m8f
	The texts of a decoded r2007+ LTYPE point into the 512 byte strings_area,
	and the DXF and DXFB writers convert them with the unbounded
	bit_convert_TU, which scans to a wide NUL. A text without one in the
	area reads past the allocation. c26f6f7c bounded only dwggrep.

	I could not reproduce it from the report. The decoder terminates the
	last 2 bytes of the area since 55442ad1c, so this is the bound the
	writers need anyway.

	Reported-by: GHSA-37w4-c8mv-7m8f reporter

	* src/bits.c (bit_TU_terminated_in_area): New.
	* src/bits.h: Declare it.
	* src/dwg.spec (LTYPE): Write the dash text in DXF only when it ends
	  in the strings_area.

2026-11-28  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	in_dxf: do not grow the SAT version of a 3DSOLID past its buffer, GHSA-6c66-qgw3-83w8
	add_3DSOLID_encr() rewrites the SAT version of the decrypted inline
	text to 400 and assumes the first space follows a version of at least 3
	digits. strtol skips leading white space though, so a decrypted text
	starting with a blank has sp at the start, and the memmove by 3 bytes
	wrote up to 3 bytes past the end of acis_data.

	Reported-by: GHSA-6c66-qgw3-83w8 reporter (fuzzing)

	* src/in_dxf.c (add_3DSOLID_encr): Only rewrite when the version field has
	  3 to 6 digits and starts at the beginning of the string.
	  Fix the bound of the "^ " lookahead: i + 1 < total.

2026-11-28  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	in_dxf: skip empty 310 preview chunks, GHSA-jqp7-x35p-3wvx
	A 310 value that decodes to zero bytes (invalid hex) made
	add_ent_preview() call realloc (preview, 0) for the first chunk. That
	frees the buffer and returns NULL, the function returned with the freed
	pointer still in the entity: a double free in dwg_free.

	Reported-by: GHSA-jqp7-x35p-3wvx reporter (fuzzing)

	* src/in_dxf.c (add_ent_preview): Skip chunks of length 0.

