2026-11-28  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	examples/unknown.pi: run the field packing solver
	The packing of the fields with several found positions was a TODO. Now
	pack/1 solves it with the picat cp module: no overlaps, the order of the
	fields, and the smallest gaps. It first tries in order, then not in
	order, and takes a quick solution if the optimization times out.

	Fields are searched only in their stream: the handles in the handle
	stream, the strings in the string stream (r2007+), all others in the
	main stream. A match across two streams was bogus.

	* examples/unknown.pi (go): Compute the three stream ranges from the
	  offsets. The result is printed behind "Most probable result:", which
	  make unknown greps for, without the TODO.
	  (stream_range, pack, pack_try, pack_set): New.
	* Makefile.am (unknown): Give picat 1m, not 30s.
	* configure.ac: Add TIMEOUT_60.

