2026-11-26  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	DXF: export r2007+ $CMLSTYLE as UTF-8, not raw TU
	HEADER_HANDLE_NAME0 printed the resolved table record name directly
	with fprintf %s. For r2007+ DWGs MLINESTYLE.name is a TU wide string
	("S\0T\0A\0..."), so %s stopped at the first embedded NUL and
	$CMLSTYLE was exported as "S" instead of "STANDARD". The deferred
	name resolution in dxf2dwg then failed, and the re-encoded DWG lost
	the CMLSTYLE handle ((5.0.0) instead of (5.1.13)).

	Route the resolved-object path through dxf_cvt_tablerecord(), which
	converts TU to UTF-8 like FIELD_HANDLE_NAME already does. Also free
	the dwg_handle_name() fallback result whenever it was allocated; the
	old code leaked it when _o0 resolved with a mismatched dxfname.

	Found by dxf-check on test/test-data/2010/5151-024.dwg, regressed
	with 23e9d5517 (r11 DXF roundtrips).

	* src/out_dxf.c (HEADER_HANDLE_NAME0): use dxf_cvt_tablerecord for
	  the object path; always free the dwg_handle_name() result

