2026-11-26  Saddam  <saddamr3e@gmail.com>

	spec: terminate the r2007+ LTYPE dash texts in strings_area
	The r2007+ dash texts are UCS-2 pointers into the 512-byte strings_area,
	which bit_read_TF terminates with a single 0 byte only. A text running to
	the end of the area had no 0 unit, so the DXF and DXFB writers read past
	the buffer in bit_convert_TU and wrote the heap bytes they found into the
	output. Clear the last unit of the area. In a valid area it is already
	0, as the terminator of the last text or padding.

	No test: it needs a crafted r2007+ DWG fixture. DXF output of the
	in-tree r2007+ DWGs is unchanged.

	* src/dwg.spec (LTYPE): Terminate the last UCS-2 text in the r2007+
	  strings_area on decode.

