2026-11-23  Saddam  <saddamr3e@gmail.com>

	in_dxf: don't let a surface profile size outgrow its 310 data
	The sweep and revolve profiles of EXTRUDEDSURFACE, REVOLVEDSURFACE,
	SWEPTSURFACE, the ACSH sweep, extrusion and revolve classes and the
	ACSH_LOFT_CLASS profiles are a size in bits (90, for the loft 94/97) and
	the 310 data. The size was only clamped to the data when the 310 run
	arrived, so a size group after the run was taken as given. The encoder
	then copied up to 64 KiB past the heap buffer into the DWG: ASan
	heap-buffer-overflow READ in bit_write_TF via
	dwg_encode_EXTRUDEDSURFACE_private, also via the REVOLVEDSURFACE,
	SWEPTSURFACE and ACSH_SWEEP_CLASS encoders.

	No testcase: it needs a crafted DXF. Reproducer: add a "90 524288" pair
	after the AcDbExtrudedSurface 310 run of test/test-data/2004/Surface.dxf
	and run dxf2dwg --as r2007.

	* src/in_dxf.c (dxf_acsh_sweep_size, dxf_surface_size): After its data,
	  do not raise the size above the clamped value.
	  (new_object): Likewise for the ACSH_LOFT_CLASS profile size.

