2026-11-23  nameloCmaS  <namelocmas@gmail.com>

	encode_test: the r2004 container as AutoCAD writes it
	Walks the r2004+ container of AutoCAD's files in test-data
	(example_2004 - example_2018, AutoCAD 2018's saves, and 2013/Arc,
	AutoCAD 2013's, with gaps) and of the encoder's output of the same
	drawings, also r2018 saved as r2004 and r2010. The sections are read
	with decompress_R2004_section, byte by byte, so the checks do not
	depend on the host's endianness:

	- bytes 0xEC..0xFF of the file header are the magic sequence;
	- the encoder writes no gaps and no gap tree;
	- the empty section 0 is first in the section map;
	- AcDb:Classes: the size counts the bytes after the size words, the
	  r2010+ high size word is 0, then the CRC, the end sentinel and 8 zero
	  bytes;
	- AcDb:AcDbObjects starts with 0x0dca;
	- AcDb:Handles pages are at most 2032 bytes, each with its CRC;
	- the encoder's output is read back with all its objects.

	maint_version and app_maint_version are 0xff in AutoCAD LT 2027's save
	to an older release (2007/block_acad2027.dwg) and in the encoder's
	r2004 - r2013 output of an r2018 drawing, not in its r2018 output.

	AutoCAD's files pass all checks. With master's encoder 10 of the 17 new
	checks fail, every rule at least once.

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

2026-11-23  nameloCmaS  <namelocmas@gmail.com>

	encode: r2004 file header and section map as AutoCAD writes them
	- no gap tree: the pages are written without gaps;
	- the empty section 0 first in the section map;
	- the section info of every written section type;
	- the bytes 0xEC..0xFF of the header from the magic sequence;
	- maint_version and app_maint_version 0xff when saving to an older
	  release (r2004-r2013), as AutoCAD does.

