2026-11-22  nameloCmaS  <namelocmas@gmail.com>

	encode_r2007: write the container as AutoCAD does
	- the sections in AutoCAD's order (ODA writes SummaryInfo first and
	  FileDepList last);
	- the unused bytes of a page filled with the padding of the file's
	  random_seed: the first 0x80 words of its random table (ODA spec
	  5.11), little endian, repeated every 512 bytes, not zeros;
	- raw pages (encoding 1) Reed-Solomon coded too, not interleaved: the
	  data padded to 8 with zeros, then the 4 parity bytes of each block
	  of 251 data bytes, the last block completed with the padding for
	  the parity, then the padding. A raw page has the Reed-Solomon coded
	  size of its section's max_size (max_size and 4 parity bytes per
	  block of 251, rounded to 32), as in all of AutoCAD's r2007 files.
	  AutoCAD 2027 rejects an AppInfoHistory page without the parity and
	  crashes on a raw page of only ROUND32 (data) bytes;
	- the mirrored CRC of the file header from a new chain, each element
	  from the one before (ODA spec 5.2.1.1.5);
	- the sections map: page sizes as allocation sizes (at least the
	  section's max size), and the empty section at the end, without a
	  name, counted in num_sections.
	AutoCAD needs these to read LibreDWG's r2007 output, but they are not
	enough on their own: with only these AutoCAD LT 2027 opens none of 12
	test-data drawings rewritten as r2007. With the other encoder changes
	of the full set (string, class and object sections), 9 of the 12 open,
	8 of them AUDIT-clean; the drawings from R2000 and R2004 sources do
	not open yet.

	Test: encode_r2007_test (new, in check_minimal next to encode_test)
	includes encode_r2007.c and decode_r2007.c:
	- the section order, pad_fill, raw_page_size, the raw pages of
	  make_data_page and the sections map;
	- every page of three AutoCAD r2007 files (2007/block_acad2027.dwg
	  from AutoCAD LT 2027, 2007/Line.dwg, example_2007.dwg), found with
	  the decoder's own map readers: the Reed-Solomon parity of each block
	  of every page, and for the raw pages (AppInfoHistory, AppInfo,
	  Preview) their size and padding, with each file's random_seed;
	- the same for the encoder's output with a 1240-byte AppInfoHistory,
	  which is read back unchanged.
	With the previous encoder 26 of its checks fail; AutoCAD's files pass
	either way.

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

2026-11-22  nameloCmaS  <namelocmas@gmail.com>

	r2007: the class dwg_version and maint_version are BL
	As in r2004 and r2010+: AutoCAD's r2007 files store them as BL
	(e.g. MLEADERSTYLE with maint_version 427). Reading them as BS takes
	the wrong number of bits for values of 256 and more, and every class
	after such a class is misread (e.g. ACDBSECTIONVIEWSTYLE with
	dwg_version 64680 and 256 instances). The encoder writes them as BL
	too.

	Tests:
	- decode_test: test-data/2007/block_acad2027.dwg, AutoCAD LT 2027's
	  r2007 save of r2.10/block.dxf, has MLEADERSTYLE maint_version 427;
	  its classes are read as AutoCAD wrote them.
	- encode_test: an r2007 class dwg_version above 0xFFFF, which no BS
	  holds, is read back.

