2026-11-21  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	classes: promote NURBSURFACE to unstable, allow DXF
	The fields (the 3DSOLID fields, u_isolines, v_isolines and, since r2013,
	short170, cv_hull_display, uvec1, vvec1, uvec2, vvec2) are right: the DXF
	roundtrip of 2018/nurbsurface.dwg and of the 4 NURBSURFACEs of
	2018/Surface.dwg keeps all of them.

	The wireframe is not in the DXF, by design
	------------------------------------------
	Every ACIS based entity (3DSOLID, REGION, BODY and the *SURFACEs) has two
	parts in the DWG:

	 1. The ACIS body (SAB, or SAT v1 before r2013): the real geometry. It is
	    written to the DXF as the SAT lines (groups 1 and 3), and read back.
	 2. A cached wireframe for display: point (the 3BD, group none), the
	    isolines count, the wires[] (type, selection_marker, color,
	    acis_index, points, transform) and the silhouettes[]. The viewers draw
	    these without a modeler, which is why the DWG has them.

	The DXF has no group codes for part 2, neither do AutoCAD nor ODA write
	it: their DXF has just AcDbModelerGeometry (the SAT) and the surface
	subclass. When AutoCAD or ODA load such a DXF or DWG without the cache
	(wireframe_data_present = 0), they recalculate the wires, isolines and
	silhouettes from the ACIS body with their modeler. That is why
	dxf-check of nurbsurface.dwg passes ODA with no wireframe, and no field
	value is lost: only the cache is.

	So the wires, silhouettes, point, isoline_present and isolines of
	Surface.dwg (12 wires per surface) are lost on DWG -> DXF -> DWG, and
	come back as wireframe_data_present: 0, point_present: 0. They are kept
	by DWG -> DWG (dwgrewrite) and JSON. It is the same for EXTRUDEDSURFACE
	and all the others, not specific to NURBSURFACE.

	Recalculating the cache would need an ACIS evaluator: for a NURBSURFACE
	the SAT has the knots, degrees and control points, so the isolines are
	plain NURBS evaluations at u_isolines x v_isolines. Trimmed solids and
	their silhouettes need a real kernel. OpenCascade cannot import ACIS, so it
	does not help. Only our own renderers (dwg2SVG, dwg2ps, GeoJSON) would
	profit, AutoCAD and ODA do not need it.

	* src/classes.inc, objects.in, objects.c: unstable, with DXF in/out.
	* src/dwg2.spec: out of the debug-only area, without the unknown bits.
	* test/unit-testing/nurbsurface.c: not only with DEBUG_CLASSES.
	* NEWS, TODO, doc.

	dxf-check of nurbsurface passes (ODA reads it, no lost fields).

