	Guard against incomplete BLOCK_HEADERs and objects from JSON/DXF imports
	Follow-up of GHSA-vj62-wp5x-vw7v, comment 382065: a BLOCK_HEADER
	reconstructed from JSON or DXF may lack its parent or its object data,
	and the walkers and writers dereferenced these unchecked (SEGV at
	dwg_next_object via dxfb_block_write, NULL deref in the MLINESTYLE
	encoder, and the table walk).

	* src/dwg.c (dwg_next_object): NULL for an object without parent or
	  without the object array. Also compare against num_objects directly,
	  (num_objects - 1) underflowed for an empty array.
	  (owned_block_header): New. get_first_owned_entity,
	  get_next_owned_entity, get_first_owned_block, get_next_owned_block,
	  get_next_owned_block_entity and get_last_owned_block return NULL for
	  an incomplete header. get_first/next_owned_subentity check the owner,
	  and the pre-R2000 branches the next object, which is NULL at the end
	  of the array.
	* src/out_dxf.c, src/out_dxfb.c: dxf_block_write and dxfb_block_write
	  skip an incomplete BLOCK_HEADER with a non-critical error. The
	  generated DWG_ENTITY and DWG_OBJECT entry points check tio.entity
	  and tio.object like out_json already does, before emitting a record.
	  The BLOCK_CONTROL of the table walk is checked, and the initializer
	  of the dead VX_CONTROL block.
	* src/out_geojson.c: check the object data of the INSERT block header.
	* src/dwg.spec (MLINESTYLE): the header LTYPE_BYBLOCK, BYLAYER and
	  CONTINUOUS handles may be missing in an imported file.
	* test/unit-testing/add_test.c (test_incomplete_block_header): New.
	  Walkers on a header without parent and without object data, and the
	  ASCII and binary DXF writers on a drawing with an incomplete header.
	  Crashed before.
	* NEWS: Document.

