2026-11-18  Saddam  <saddamr3e@gmail.com>

	in_json, in_dxf: keep OLE2FRAME.cfb_size in sync with data
	OLE2FRAME.data holds only the MS-CFB, and the DWG, JSON and DXF
	writers copy cfb_size bytes from it. The DWG decoder bounds cfb_size,
	but the importers did not tie it to the buffer: a JSON cfb_size key
	was kept as given next to a shorter hex data string, and a second DXF
	90 reallocated data but kept the cfb_size of the previous 310 stream.
	Both overread the heap into the written DWG.

	* src/in_json.c (_set_struct_field): Set cfb_size from the data
	  length, and ignore the cfb_size key, like sab_size.
	* src/in_dxf.c (new_object): Reset cfb_size with a new 90 buffer.

	No testcase: a JSON or DXF OLE2FRAME needs a CFB payload, which
	would exceed the 15 lines that do not need a copyright assignment.

