2026-11-15  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	encode_r2007: CRCs, compression, ODA reads the container
	The r2007 writer now sets all the check values of ODA spec ch. 5:
	the 64-bit CRCs (normal ECMA-182 and mirrored, with the byte order of
	the 2 byte words of the 8 byte blocks), the 32-bit data page checksum,
	the pseudo random encoder for the seeds and the check data of the
	file header, the hashcodes of the sections, the system page sizes and
	repeat counts. All formulas are verified against example_2007.dwg.

	The r2007 LZ77 compressor, the inverse of decompress_r2007, is new, with
	the permuted literal runs. Compressed are the data pages, the system
	pages and the file header.

	ODAFileConverter reads such a file, if the objects are converted
	properly. Known:
	* TABLESTYLE converted from r2010+ is rejected by ODA.
	* Rewriting an r2007 DWG as r2007 keeps stale object sizes, so
	  dwgrewrite still writes r2010 for those.

	* src/encode_r2007.c: the above. The section names are zero terminated
	  and the sections amount is +1, the sections in the order of ODA, the
	  addresses of the preview, summaryinfo and appinfo are set.
	* src/encode.c: the r2010 bitsize_hi word is not written for r2007.
	  compress_R2004_section is static again.
	* programs/dxf2dwg.c: allow r2007.
	* test/unit-testing/encode_test.c: compress_r2007 roundtrip and an r2007
	  encode and decode test.
	* NEWS, TODO, doc/LibreDWG.texi.

2026-11-15  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	WIP encode_r2007: write the r2007 container, ODA rejects it
	dwg_encode fell back to r2010 for r2007. Now src/encode_r2007.c writes
	the r2007 file from the section buffers of the r2004+ path: the 0x400
	file header (3 Reed-Solomon (255,239) blocks), the pages map and the
	sections map, repeated twice, the data pages Reed-Solomon (255,251)
	coded, and the copy of the file header. Uses rs_encode_block and
	rs_encode_data_block.

	LibreDWG reads such a file back: same 208 objects and 17 classes as the
	r2010 JSON it was written from. ODAFileConverter rejects it with "CRC
	does not match", because the CRC64 and the checksums of the file header,
	the system pages and the section pages are zero. Their algorithms are not
	known. Plain CRC64 variants (ECMA, ISO, Jones, XZ, with the seeds and
	data of the header) do not match the values of example_2007.dwg.

	* The pages and the file header are stored uncompressed. The LZ77 of
	  r2007 is not that of r2004: compress_R2004_section output fails
	  decompress_r2007 for 300 of 300 random buffers (the r2007 literals are
	  stored in permuted 8 byte groups). ACadSharp has no r2007 writer, its
	  AC21 file header writer is a stub and its AC21 compressor throws.
	* encode.c: no fallback to r2010. compress_R2004_section is exported.
	  Fix the EED strings of r2007, the pre-r2007 format was written for
	  r2007 also, and the bitsize_hi word of the header section, which
	  r2007 does not have.
	* dxf2dwg and dwgwrite still do not advertise r2007.

