2026-11-15  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	decode_r2007: correct the Reed-Solomon errors of the pages
	decode_rs only de-interleaved the blocks, and dropped the parity bytes,
	the call of rs_decode_block was disabled. Now every block of the system
	pages (255,239) and the data pages (255,251) is decoded, errors are
	corrected and uncorrectable blocks are warned about.

	* src/reedsolomon.c: the code is generic now, with the (255,251) code of
	  the data pages, primitive polynomial 0x11d, 4 parity bytes, corrects 2
	  errors: rs_encode_data_block, rs_decode_data_block. Same roots
	  alpha^1.. and layout as the system pages.
	* src/decode_r2007.c (decode_rs): decode each block. Only with the full 255
	  bytes per block in the page, else as before.

	Verified with the 33 r2007 test DWGs: all 516 data and 23 system blocks of
	example_2007.dwg are valid codewords, and no file has a block with errors,
	so the parameters of the data pages (0x11d, roots alpha^1) are right. A
	flipped byte in a data page is corrected in 11 of 30 random positions
	(the others are not RS coded), and the JSON is the same as of the clean file.

	* decode_test: a flipped byte of example_2007.dwg gives the same objects.
	  It fails without the correction.
	* bits_test: (255,251) blocks.

	ACadSharp (../ACadSharp, DwgReader.reedSolomonDecoding) also only
	de-interleaves the blocks, with the same strides and block sizes (239 for
	the system and 251 for the data pages), and has no error correction.

2026-11-15  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	reedsolomon: a new implementation of the (255,239) code
	Replaces the unused code which was written by Alex Papazoglou, for
	which we have no copyright assignment, by a new one written from the
	textbook algorithms: syndromes, Berlekamp-Massey, Chien search and
	Forney's formula. Same field (0x169), roots alpha^1..alpha^16 and
	block layout.

	* src/reedsolomon.c, reedsolomon.h: same API, rs_encode_block and
	  rs_decode_block. It encodes the same parity as the old code (compared
	  with the old code for random blocks of 0..239 bytes) and corrects up to
	  8 errors in a block, where the old one failed at 8. More than 8 errors
	  are rejected.
	* bits_test: encode/decode 40 blocks with 0..8 errors, 9 errors, and a
	  short block against its zero-padded one.
	* TODO: drop the reed-solomon item. NEWS.

