2026-11-15  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	mmap: fix Windows file mapping for reads and overshoot
	Windows file views cannot extend past EOF: CreateFileMapping rejects a
	section larger than the file, and MapViewOfFile(Ex) rejects a view larger
	than the section.  The previous code tried to map size+64KiB for every
	read, which always failed on Windows.

	- dat_mmap_read: only request overshoot for the DXF append path
	  (dat_read_size), where chain[size] and chain[size+1] may be written.
	  DWG reads (dat_read_file) map exactly the file size so Windows can use
	  a real file view.
	- mman.c mmap(): when len > filesize on a MAP_PRIVATE map, fall back to
	  calloc+ReadFile - identical semantics (zeroed tail, private writes).
	- Replace MapViewOfFileEx+VirtualAlloc with MapViewOfFile: the former
	  requires 64KiB-aligned base which VirtualAlloc does not guarantee.

2026-11-15  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	mmap: cap section size at file size on Windows
	CreateFileMapping fails with ERROR_NOT_ENOUGH_MEMORY when the section
	size exceeds the file size for PAGE_WRITECOPY/PAGE_READWRITE.  Cap
	maxsize at the file size; MapViewOfFileEx into reserved address space
	still provides the full len bytes.

	mmap: log CreateFileMapping/MapViewOfFileEx errors
	Still failing on MinGW/MSVC - need the actual Win32 error code to
	diagnose whether CreateFileMapping or MapViewOfFileEx rejects the
	beyond-EOF view.

	mmap: make dwg_fstat_size a real function
	static in header caused unused-function warnings (bits.c doesn't call
	it) and -Werror=inline on mips. Define once in mman.c, declare in
	mmap.h; mman.h now included unconditionally.

	mmap: drop inline on dwg_fstat_size
	static inline fails -Werror=inline on mips32 (call is unlikely and
	code size would grow).

	my_stat: use io.h for _access on MSVC
	io.h declares _access with C linkage; the manual decl conflicted with
	UCRT (C2375). access() callers need the declaration too.

	my_stat: declare _access with C linkage on MSVC
	mman.h now pulls in <sys/stat.h> -> UCRT io.h which declares _access
	with C linkage; the previous C++-linkage decl in my_stat.h conflicted
	(C2375). Keep the access() macro - programs use it.

	my_stat: drop redundant _access decl on MSVC
	mman.h now includes <sys/stat.h> on Windows, which pulls in the UCRT
	io.h that already declares _access with C linkage; the manual
	declaration here conflicted (C2375 different linkage). access() is
	unused in the tree.

	mman: fix Windows/MSVC/MinGW build and beyond-EOF mappings
	* src/mman.h: include proper headers per platform; add dwg_mmap_off_t
	  (off_t is absent on MSVC, 32-bit on 32-bit MinGW); MSVC fileno/ftruncate
	  shims; dwg_fstat_size() helper avoiding struct stat/_stat differences.
	* src/mman.c: mmap() signature uses dwg_mmap_off_t; map via
	  VirtualAlloc(MEM_RESERVE)+MapViewOfFileEx so views may extend past EOF
	  (read path maps size+64KiB for its append overshoot) - pages past EOF
	  fault in as zero like POSIX private maps; munmap decommits+releases.
	* src/bits.c, src/dwg.c: guard unistd.h includes; use dwg_fstat_size()
	  instead of fstat/struct stat; keep dat_mmap_read defined without
	  DWG_HAVE_MMAP.
	* src/cmakeconfig.h.in: add missing HAVE_SYS_MMAN_H cmakedefine.
	* test/unit-testing: link mman.c/mman.lo into tests that compile
	  bits.c/dwg.c directly.

