2026-11-15  Saddam  <saddamr3e@gmail.com>

	encode: use the \U+ expanded TU length for T16, EED and xdata
	Since deea2c4 bit_utf8_to_TU expands \U+XXXX and \M+xxxxx escapes
	before the conversion, so the result has fewer chars than strlen() of
	the input and is allocated only that long. The r2007+ TV branch of
	bit_write_T16, the TV EED and xdata string writers, and the r2007+ xdata
	import of DXF and JSON still took the char count from strlen() of the
	UTF-8 input, and copied the heap bytes past the converted string into
	the written DWG.

	* src/bits.c (bit_write_T16): Take the length from the converted string.
	* src/encode.c (dwg_encode_eed_data, dwg_encode_xdata): Clamp to the
	  converted length, not strlen.
	* src/in_dxf.c (add_xdata): Set the r2007+ xdata string size to the
	  converted length.
	* src/in_json.c (json_xdata): Likewise.
	* test/unit-testing/bits_test.c (bit_write_TV_tests): Add a \U+ T16
	  check.

