2026-11-15  garcialeal  <garcialeal2@gmail.com>

	dwg2SVG: place INSERTs right
	A block was written in page coordinates, and its <use> moved it again by
	the insertion point, so the page offset was added twice: every INSERT
	was out of place, often off the page.  Its rotation also turned the
	wrong way, as y is flipped, and a mirrored OCS was ignored.

	Blocks are now written in their own coordinates from their base point,
	and the <use> of an INSERT is translate(insertion point) scale(-1 1)
	for a mirrored OCS, rotate(-rotation) and scale(x y).  The page is
	written as before.

	* programs/dwg2SVG.c (transform_X, transform_Y): Use origin_x, origin_y
	and origin_h.
	(block_origin): New.
	(output_INSERT): Turn the rotation, and mirror x for a mirrored OCS.
	(output_SVG): Set the origin of the page and of each block.
	* test/test-data/2000/Inserts.dxf: New, made with ezdxf.
	* test/Makefile.am: Add it.
	* programs/svg.test.in: Check a rotated INSERT of 2000/entities-2d.dwg
	and the INSERTs of 2000/Inserts.dxf.

