2026-11-10  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	bits: unescape \U+/\M+ in bit_utf8_to_TU
	bit_utf8_to_TU converts UTF-8 input to the stored UCS-2 (BITCODE_TU)
	form for the add path (dwg_add_u8_input, in_dxf, in_json, encode).
	For R2007+ DWG (IS_FROM_TU) the stored UCS-2 MTEXT is written verbatim
	to DXF by the VALUE_TU path (bit_convert_TU, no bit_u_expand), so a
	literal \U+XXXX / \M+xxxxx escape sequence stayed literal in the
	output instead of expanding to the actual glyph.

	Expand the escape sequences at the point the string is converted into
	UCS-2, the same way AutoCAD decodes them and the way bit_TV_to_utf8
	already does on the TV path. Run bit_u_expand on a copy of the input
	because it shrinks in place and str is the caller's restrict buffer;
	it is a no-op for strings without a real \U+ / \M+ sequence.

	* src/bits.c (bit_utf8_to_TU): expand \U+XXXX / \M+xxxxx to the
	  actual UTF-8 characters before the UTF-8->UCS-2 conversion.

	GH #1414

