2026-11-09  Mar Dominguez  <mardgez13@gmail.com>

	in_dxf: read $DWGCODEPAGE in the width dynapi stored it
	dxf_set_DWGCODEPAGE guessed a TU name from a 0 second byte once
	header.version is r2007+. But an imported $DWGCODEPAGE is TV: dynapi
	stores a string as TU only if IS_FROM_TU_DWG, which is never the case
	for a DXF import (and when it chose by header.version, that was still
	R_INVALID while the HEADER of an r2007+ DXF is read). So a
	one-character name is a 2-byte TV, and bit_convert_TU read it 2 bytes
	past its end (heap-buffer-overflow). Decide by IS_FROM_TU_DWG, as
	dynapi does.

	* src/in_dxf.c (dxf_set_DWGCODEPAGE): Read the name as TU only if
	  IS_FROM_TU_DWG.

