2026-11-09  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	acds: read and write the SAB data of ACIS entities, r2013+
	AutoCAD r2013+ keeps the SAB data of the ACIS entities (3DSOLID, REGION,
	BODY, surfaces) in the AcDb:AcDsPrototype_1b section, not in the entity,
	which has only has_ds_data. We found the SAB only by searching the
	section for an "ACIS BinaryFile" header, which AutoCAD does not write,
	it writes "ASM BinaryFile4", so all those entities stayed empty. We did
	not write the section either, and the ACDSDATA section of the DXF was
	ignored on import, not written on export. The geometry was silently
	lost in each conversion.

	Read the data records by the handle: the data index entries point to
	the record headers (size, 1, handle, local offset) of the _data_
	segments, the data starts at the object data alignment offset of the
	segment, with an UInt32 size, or the marker 0xBB106BB1 for a blob
	reference to the pages in blob01 segments (data > 0x40000). Records
	which are not for a ACIS entity we have, i.e. the thumbnail PNG, or an
	entity we cannot decode, are kept in acds.records, to be written back.

	Write the section from the entities when encoding to r2013+: the
	segidx, datidx, _data_, schidx, schdat and search segments, the schema
	segments are constant. The result for example_2018.dwg is identical to
	AutoCAD's section, byte by byte. With blob01 pages the order of the
	segments is as ODA writes it. The entities then have has_ds_data and
	the acis_empty_bit set.

	The DXF r2013+ has the SAB in the ACDSDATA section, with the constant
	ACDSSCHEMA elements and an ACDSRECORD per entity with the handle 320
	and the data 310, and an empty entity. Read and write it, also as
	binary DXF.

	Checked with ODAFileConverter: it reads our section of example_2018, of
	a DXF REGION by ezdxf, and with large data in blob01 pages (0.3 and 1.2
	MB), and we read ODA's sections with blob pages. The issue reproducer
	(ezdxf REGION, dxf2dwg --as r2018, dwg2dxf) now has the 5489 bytes SAB
	and the ACDSDATA.

	The SAB cannot be written to R2000 and older, we convert it to SAT v1
	there, as the DXF export does. The ASM SAB of r2013+ cannot be converted
	to the SAT or to older versions, and is not written there. SAT v1 data
	cannot be converted to SAB, and is not written to r2013+.

	* include/dwg.h (Dwg_AcDs_Record): New, the other data records.
	  (Dwg_AcDs): Add num_records, records.
	  (Dwg_Data): Remove the temporary acis_sab_hdl.
	  (dwg_obj_get_sab, dwg_obj_set_sab): New.
	* src/acds.c: New. acds_assign_sab reads the data records into the
	  entities, acds_collect_records lists the records to write.
	* src/acds.h: New.
	* src/acds.spec: No search for the SAB, see acds.c.
	* src/decode.c, src/decode_r2007.c (read_*_section_acds): Call
	  acds_assign_sab, also with a damaged later segment.
	* src/encode_acds.c: New, encode_acds writes the section.
	* src/encode.c (encode_r2004): Write the SECTION_ACDS, compressed.
	* src/common_entity_data.spec: Set has_ds_data from the SAB data.
	* src/dwg_spec_shared.h (encode_3dsolid): Set the acis_empty_bit for
	  r2013+, convert the SAB to SAT v1 for r2000-, no ASM SAB before r2013.
	  (free_3dsolid): Free block_size and encr_sat_data also with acis_empty,
	  which the encoder sets for the data it cannot write.
	* src/dwg.c (dwg_obj_get_sab, dwg_obj_set_sab): New.
	* src/free.c: Free the records, and no acis_sab_hdl.
	* src/out_dxf.c, src/out_dxfb.c (dxf_acds_write): The ACDSDATA section.
	  (dxf_3dsolid, dxfb_3dsolid): No data in the entity for r2013+.
	* src/in_dxf.c (dxf_acds_read): Read the ACDSDATA section.
	* src/Makefile.am, CMakeLists.txt: Add acds.c and encode_acds.c.
	* test/unit-testing/encode_test.c (acds_sab_test): New, 3 REGIONs, one
	  in a blob, roundtripped.
	* test/unit-testing/Makefile.am (decode_test_LDADD, encode_test_LDADD):
	  Add acds.lo, encode_acds.lo.
	* test/unit-testing/CMakeLists.txt (decode_test): Add acds.c.

