2026-11-08  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	TABLE: the pre-R2007 cell alignment is a BS, not a RS
	An AC1015 TABLE with cell overrides was decoded wrongly after the first
	cell with an alignment override: the cells got garbage, and decoding
	ended with "Invalid ACAD_TABLE.cells x 24" or buffer overflows, leaving
	the rest of the entity as unknown bits.

	The cell alignment, present with bit 0x01 of the cell flag override, is
	a bitshort, as the other values around it, not a raw short as the ODA
	spec says. Checked on the table.dwg of GH #1062 (6 columns x 4 rows, 24
	cells, overrides in many cells, in AC1015): all cells now decode with
	the same texts, flags, merges, text heights (2.0, 1.5) and alignments as
	ODAFileConverter reads them (it only omits the default alignment 1), no
	errors, and a dwgrewrite roundtrip reads back the same.

	The regeneration also moves TABLE to the stable objects in dwg_api.h
	and objects.in, which was missed with the TABLE class made stable for
	the DXF.

	* include/dwg.h (Dwg_TABLE_Cell): cell_alignment is a BITCODE_BS.
