2026-11-08  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	tablestyle: read the three R2010+ cell styles, convert both ways
	The R2010+ TABLESTYLE has, after the "Table" cell style, a count (3) and
	then the title, header and data cell styles. We read the count as
	numoverrides and then only one cell style (ovr), with a misplaced
	unknown_bl3. That left 6688 bits unread in example_2018, and made the
	down- and up-conversion guess: the title style was written as the data
	rowstyle, the margins were lost, the border order, invisibility and fill
	color were wrong.

	Each entry is the cell style id (1 title, 2 header, 3 data), the cell
	style (type 5, as the Table style), the cell style id again, the class
	and the name (_TITLE, _HEADER, _DATA). The first id is always the same
	as the last one: checked in all 141 R2010+ sample files, always 3
	styles. The main stream now ends exactly at the start of the string
	stream.

	Checked against AutoCAD's own files: the rowstyles downconverted from
	example_2018 are identical to the native example_2000 rowstyles in every
	field, the cell styles upconverted from example_2000 are identical to
	the example_2018 cell styles, and a same-version rewrite is identical.

	* include/dwg.h (Dwg_Object_TABLESTYLE): Replace numoverrides,
	  unknown_bl3 and ovr by num_cellstyles and cellstyles.
	* src/dwg2.spec (TABLESTYLE): Read the cell styles. Not in the DXF,
	  where they only exist in the CELLSTYLEMAP. flow_direction is 0 or 1.
	  Downconvert before the margins are written.
	* src/encode.c (downconvert_TABLESTYLE): Use the cell styles by id, map
	  the border edge flags to the rowstyle border order, invert the
	  invisibility, use the table cell style margins, default fill color as
	  AutoCAD. Do not share strings, copy non-global handles.
	  (upconvert_TABLESTYLE): Write the three cell styles from the rowstyles
	  and the AutoCAD defaults for the Table cell style.
	* src/free.c (free_TABLESTYLE_r2010): Simplified.
	  (free_TABLESTYLE_upconverted): New, free() follows from_version.
