	encode: downconvert R2010+ TABLE to the pre-R2010 cells
	Writing a R2010+ TABLE as R2000-R2007 produced an empty table
	(0 columns, 0 rows), because the pre-R2010 branch of the spec only looks
	at the old cell fields, while the R2010+ data is kept in the table
	content (LinkedTableData). downconvert_TABLE existed, but was never
	called, read the cell text from the wrong field, and the columns stayed
	unset.

	R2010+ stores the cell strings as UTF-16LE bytes in value.data_date, not
	as value.data_string. Merged cells follow what AutoCAD writes itself in
	example_2000.dwg: the top left cell holds the extent (merged_width_flag
	x merged_height_flag), the covered cells have is_merged_value set.

	The converted table of example_2010/2013/2018 is identical to the native
	example_2000 table: 20 rows x 9 columns, same cell texts, merge, widths,
	heights, flag_for_table_value 0x16 and horiz_direction.

	* src/dwg2.spec (TABLE): Call downconvert_TABLE when encoding a TABLE
	  that came from R2010+ to <R2010.
	* src/encode.c (downconvert_TABLE): Check obj before use. Skip tables
	  which have pre-R2010 cells already. Convert column widths, row heights,
	  text (or block with scale and attribute texts) of the first cell
	  content and merged cells. Set horiz_direction and the table flag.
	  Strings keep the TU/TV flavour of the source.
	  (table_dup_T, table_ascii_to_T, table_value_text): New helpers.
