	  R2010+ spec does not know. Like free_TABLESTYLE_r2010, free() follows
	  from_version, not version. Found with valgrind.
	* test/unit-testing/encode_test.c (downconvert_TABLE_test): New.

	Not converted: cell styles, formats, borders, additional cell contents.

2026-11-08  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	decode: cap the REPEAT size check per element; read r2010+ tables
	REPEAT_CHKCOUNT compares count * sizeof (struct), as a number of bits,
	with the remaining bits. The memory size of a struct is no wire bound:
	a Dwg_TableRow holds many pointers, so the r2010+ TABLEs of
	example_2010/2013/2018 were rejected (Invalid ACAD_TABLE.tdata.rows) and
	left as unknown bits. Cap the per-element size at 32, which only
	loosens the check. The unit stays one bit per struct byte, a stricter
	bound would reject valid small repeats (MLINE lines, evaluation graph
	nodes), leaking what was already allocated.

	With this the r2010+ tables decode fully: insert data, the table
	content (columns, rows, cells), the horizontal direction and the break
	data, ending with a verified CRC and no leftover. Checked on
	example_2010/2013/2018.

	Part of GH #1446. The rest of it (the r2010+ TABLESTYLE cell styles,
	downconvert_TABLE, ACAD_TABLE in DXF) needs the ODA 20.4.101 layout and
	is not in this commit.

	* src/dec_macros.h (REPEAT_CHKCOUNT, REPEAT_CHKCOUNT_LVAL): Cap the
	  per-element size at 32.

2026-11-08  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	in_dxf: rename scan variable to avoid shadow

2026-11-08  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	in_dxf: join MTEXT text chunks before codepage conversion
	The text of an MTEXT entity is split into 250-char chunks: code 3 for
	the leading chunks and code 1 for the last one. dxf_read_pair converts
	each r2007+ UTF-8 string to the pre-r2007 target codepage on its own, so
	a multi-byte character that spans a chunk boundary was corrupted
	("∅" read back as "âˆ…", "隔日" as mojibake).

	Keep the chunks as raw UTF-8 while reading (dxf_mtext_text) and convert
	the joined text once at the end of the entity, like dxf_pair_string
	does for the other text fields. A r2007+ target keeps the UTF-8;
	bit_write_T converts it to TU.

