2026-11-07  garcialeal  <garcialeal2@gmail.com>

	geom: reject HATCH rings with non-finite or degenerate data
	hatch_path_points converted the number of arc steps to int even for a
	NaN angle or radius from a corrupt DWG, which is undefined behaviour
	(UBSan: "nan is outside the range of representable values of type
	'int'"), and wrote "nan" coordinates, which is no valid JSON.  It also
	accepted rings of zero area, like three points on a line.  Now a
	non-finite arc makes the whole ring unusable, rather than a ring
	without that arc, and a ring needs finite coordinates and a non-zero
	area relative to its size.

	* src/geom.c (ring_add_ellipse_sweep): Reject non-finite parameters,
	and bound the step count before the conversion to int.
	(ring_is_usable): New.
	(ring_finish): Use it.
	* test/unit-testing/geom_test.c (hatch_path_tests): Test a NaN angle,
	an infinite radius and a zero area.

