	geojson: write HATCH as Polygon or MultiPolygon
	HATCH entities were not written at all.  Each boundary path becomes a
	closed ring by hatch_path_points; its nesting depth, from point in
	polygon tests, and the HATCH style decide what is filled: Normal fills
	by parity, an island in a hole being an area again, Outer fills the
	outermost area with its holes, and Ignore the outermost area only.  The
	boundaries around texts are skipped.  One area is a Polygon, several are
	a MultiPolygon, with the rings oriented as in RFC 7946.  All 33 HATCHes
	of the test DWGs are now written, and on a test DXF made with ezdxf the
	three styles give the expected areas.

