	geom: add hatch_path_points, polygon_area and point_in_polygon
	The boundary paths of a HATCH become closed rings of points: polylines
	with their bulges, and edges of lines, circular and elliptical arcs and
	SPLINEs, within a tolerance relative to the path size.  A clockwise arc
	or ellipse edge is defined in a mirrored system, as in DXF, which makes
	it the counter-clockwise arc from -end to -start.  Over a test DXF made
	with ezdxf, with all edge types, both arc directions and nested islands,
	the 17 rings match ezdxf's own boundary paths within 0.2% of their size.

