2026-11-06  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	encode: fix memmove of overlarge (>0x7fff) objects losing the tail
	When an object grows past 0x7fff bytes, the MS size field grows from 2
	to 4 bytes and the object is moved right by 2. The memmove length was
	size + 3, but the moved span is the MS size, the handlestream size and
	the type (obj->address - dat->byte) plus the size data bytes. Up to 3
	bytes, the end of the handle stream, were lost: the 74 KB AcDbXrecord
	0x140 of sample_2010 got a garbage reactor handle and ODA reported
	"Object improperly read". sample_2010 now passes dxf-check (RC=0).

	* src/encode.c (dwg_encode_add_object): compute the memmove length from
	  obj->address, in both the grow and shrink cases.

