2026-11-06  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	encode: ODA-compatible r2010+ output, fix header size and LZ pages
	ODA rejected every r2010/r2013/r2018 DWG we wrote with "CRC does not
	match", while r2000 and r2004 passed. Bisected by repacking sections
	into an ACadSharp-style container: the container was fine, only the
	AcDb:Header section content made ODA fail.

	Root cause: for r2010 (maintenance > 3) and r2018+ the Header section
	has a 4 byte bitsize_hi word after the size. ODA's size excludes that
	word, ours included it, so ODA computed the section CRC over 4 bytes
	too many. With this fixed, sample_2013 and sample_2018 pass dxf-check.

	While there, make the r2004+ section writer follow the ODA/ACadSharp
	conventions, as the compressed pages were never validated before:

	- Compress the data pages with the LZ77 compressor (a port of the
	  ACadSharp DwgLZ77AC18Compressor), per ODA: Header, Classes, Handles,
	  AcDbObjects, ObjFreeSpace, Template, RevHistory, AuxHeader. The
	  descriptors now say compressed=2 for these, 1 for raw sections.
	- Terminate every LZ stream with 0x11 0x00 0x00, not just 0x11.
	- Pad every page to a multiple of 32 bytes with the leading bytes of
	  the magic sequence. Replaces the 16-byte zero padding.
	- The data page header size field is the padded on-disk page size
	  (32 + compressed + pad), not the decompressed size.
	- The section info page entries carry the real compressed page sizes,
	  which are only known after the pages were written, so patch them in
	  before writing the Section Info page.
	- Do not write bogus nameless descriptors for the Section Info and Page
	  Map system pages, ODA would try to read them as data sections.
	- Never flag sections as encrypted, as ODA and AutoCAD do.
	- Raw sections (SummaryInfo, Preview, AppInfo, FileDepList) get one
	  page of the content size rounded up to 32, not max_decomp_size. This
	  shrinks r2004 output of a small DXF from 1.3MB to 12KB.

	The remaining ODA warnings on some r2010+ files (Invalid Layer, Color
	index 65535, an unreadable AcDbXrecord) are object encoding issues and
	no longer container ones.

	* src/encode.c (encode_header_vars): exclude bitsize_hi from the r2010+
	  header section size.
	  (section_encrypted): return 0 for all sections.
	  (section_compressed): enable, used for the descriptors.
	  (pad_R2004_page): New, pad pages to 32 with the magic sequence.
	  (store_R2004_section, stored_R2004_section_size, compress_R2004_section):
	  terminate with 0x11 0x00 0x00. Drop the HAVE_COMPRESS_R2004_SECTION
	  gate.
	  (dwg_encode): Compress data pages, size raw pages to their content,
	  pad all pages, set the page size header field, patch the info page
	  sizes, and skip the system sections in the descriptor list.

2026-11-06  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	encode: pad r2004+ section pages to 16-byte alignment
	The r2004+ section map only stores (number, size) pairs and the reader
	accumulates section addresses from 0x100, so every size but the last
	must be a multiple of 16 to keep the next section address aligned.
	Original AutoCAD and ODA files all honor this; our writer did not:

	- Preview pages were written as raw copies of 0x7fff bytes (r2013/
	  2018, max_decomp_size from GH #1045), drifting every later section
	  by 15.
	- The SECTION_INFO page (20-byte header + content) was not padded.

	Zero-pad data section pages (32 + comp_data_size) and the
	SECTION_INFO page (20 + comp_data_size) to 16-byte boundaries.
	This keeps the section addresses ODA accumulates aligned. It is a
	necessary but not sufficient fix for ODA accepting our r2010+ output;
	the residual rejection is the separate known limitation that raw-copy
	data pages are not yet ODA-compatible (the LZ compressor is #if 0'd).

	* src/encode.c (dwg_encode): pad r2004+ data pages and SECTION_INFO
	  to 16-byte boundaries before writing.

