2026-11-05  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	dwg_api: set only INDXF, not INJSON, for fresh documents
	A fresh document from dwg_add_Document (dwg_new_Document, dwgadd) sets
	DWG_OPTS_IN (= INDXF | INJSON) so that IS_FROM_TU_DWG stays false and the
	add API stores codepage (TV) strings.  Since f939c3778 "add api: convert
	the UTF-8 string args", dwg_add_u8_input already converted the UTF-8
	input to the target codepage at add time.  The INJSON bit then made
	bit_write_TV convert the already-converted TV bytes again, this time
	parsing them as UTF-8: on a fresh R2000 file, "TEST ØST" (TV "D8") was
	re-decoded as the overlong/invalid UTF-8 pair D8 53 and re-encoded as
	the escape "\U+0613", corrupting every non-ASCII character.

	After a readdwg the import flags were dropped by dwg_read_file, so the
	append path stayed correct while the fresh path corrupted.  Both were
	reported in GH #1499.

	Set only DWG_OPTS_INDXF: it still suppresses IS_FROM_TU_DWG and keeps
	the dynamic-dxfname (strdup/free) pairing of the add API, but does not
	mark the in-memory strings as UTF-8, so bit_write_TV writes them
	verbatim.  All DWG_OPTS_IN (0xC0) usesites match, as INDXF (0x40) is a
	subset; the only behavioral change is the removal of the double
	conversion.  This also avoids treating raw TV name fields of fresh
	R2007+ documents as UTF-16 in the DXF writer (heap-buffer-overflow in
	bit_convert_TU seen under ASan when INJSON/IN were dropped entirely).

	examples/dwgadd_test.sh.in:
	  * Add a GH #1499 regression test: create a fresh R2000 file with a
	    UTF-8 TEXT ("TEST ØST"), append another TEXT ("NY DØR ÆØÅ") after
	    readdwg, then check both values in the JSON dump.

