2026-11-05  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	bits: stop infinite buffer doubling on truncated UTF-8 tail
	bit_utf8_to_TV() returned NULL for a 3-byte UTF-8 lead byte at the very
	end of the input (no continuation bytes left), because all three
	sub-branches require s + 1 <= ends and the final else then returns
	NULL. Since that NULL does not depend on the destination size, callers
	looping on "grow the buffer and retry" (bit_write_TV doubles destlen
	until success) allocated 2^n bytes forever and hit a 64 GB OOM.

	* bits.c
	  - bit_utf8_to_TV: drop a stray 3-byte lead byte at the end of the
	    input and continue, like the 2-byte branch already does; only
	    return NULL for a genuinely undersized destination

