2026-11-05  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	encode: free handle stream on early entity/object exit
	oss-fuzz testcase 6080946684887040 (Direct-leak)

	The generated dwg_encode_<token>() wrappers allocated per-object
	handle (and string) streams via bit_chain_init_dat(). They were
	supposed to be freed by DWG_ENTITY_END/DWG_OBJECT_END at the end of
	the _private() function, but a _private() body can return early
	(e.g. HATCH with an invalid path segment curve_type returns 0 from
	the repeat block) and skip that epilogue. The wrapper only cleaned
	up on DWG_ERR_VALUEOUTOFBOUNDS, leaking the 128 byte hdl_dat chain
	(and the str_dat chain on R2007+) otherwise.

	bit_chain_free() NULLs the chain, so a live chain after _private()
	returns is a reliable early-exit indicator. Free both streams
	unconditionally when they are still allocated.

	* src/encode.c (DWG_ENTITY, DWG_OBJECT): free hdl_dat/str_dat when
	  still live after _private() returns

