	bit_write_T16 converts a TU source (r2007+ DWG) to codepage for a
	pre-r2007 target into a fixed char dest[1024] via bit_utf8_to_TV,
	then calls strlen (dest). bit_utf8_to_TV stops once the buffer is
	full without writing a terminator, so a string of 1024 or more
	codepage bytes (e.g. the AcDb:Template description, which the
	decoder reads without a length limit, and dwgrewrite downgrades
	r2007+ DWGs to r2004 by default) leaves dest unterminated: strlen
	reads off the stack array (ASan stack-buffer-overflow READ of size
	1030 in strlen, called from encode_template) and bit_write_RC
	copies the stack bytes behind it into the output DWG.

	Terminate dest[1023] after the conversion, as the in_dxf.c callers
	converting into the same 1024-byte dest already do, so the string
	is cut at 1023 codepage bytes.

	test/unit-testing/bits_test.c:
	- Add a bit_write_TV test writing an 1100-char TU string to a
	  pre-r2007 target and expecting the RS length 1024 (1023 chars
	  plus NUL); fails without the fix, passes with it.

