2026-11-04  garcialeal  <garcialeal2@gmail.com>

	geom: add spline_flatten, adaptive de Casteljau subdivision
	Outputs without curves need points on a SPLINE.  spline_flatten halves
	each Bezier curve of the SPLINE by de Casteljau until all its control
	points are within the tolerance of its chord, which bounds the distance
	of the curve to the polyline, as the curve lies in the convex hull of
	its control points.  SPLINEs with only fit points are interpolated
	first.  Over the 602 SPLINEs of the test DWGs the curve stays within 83%
	of the tolerance; a 10 times finer tolerance takes 2.8 times the points.

	* src/geom.c (point_list, point_list_add, segment_distance,
	bezier_is_flat, bezier_halves, bezier_flatten, points_size,
	spline_eval_points, spline_flatten): New.
	* src/geom.h (BEZIER_MAX_DEPTH, SPLINE_MAX_POINTS, SPLINE_EVAL_STEPS):
	New.  Declare spline_flatten.
	* test/unit-testing/geom_test.c (spline_flatten_tests): New.

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

