2026-11-04  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	in_dxf: skip invalid objects and continue parsing
	Many DXF files fail to parse with error 0x800 (DWG_ERR_INVALIDDWG)
	because of some exotic structure that the importer does not handle.
	Previously the import terminated on the first such object. Now it logs
	a warning with the object name, skips the rest of the object (read
	pairs until the next 0 code), and continues parsing. This allows
	drawings with a few bad objects to be partially imported, and gives
	a way of logging what went wrong to improve the importer.

	The four new_object call sites (table entries, objects, entities,
	and the objects section) are all changed to skip and continue. The
	other DWG_ERR_INVALIDDWG returns (HEADER, CLASSES, DWG-not-DXF)
	remain fatal, as they indicate a file that is not a valid DXF at all.

	Reported-by: tuxiasumari

2026-11-04  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	dwg_next_handle: scan all objects for the max seed
	The seed loop took the handle of the last object with a nonzero handle and
	stopped. That is only the maximum when objects are appended in increasing
	handle order. During a DXF import they are not: pre-created table objects
	carry high handles before the file's own low handles arrive, so fresh
	objects got handles already in use (duplicate handle errors, and the
	object map pointed two objects at one handle).

	Scan all objects for the true maximum, matching the comment and the refs
	pass below it (which already scans everything).

	Reported-by: tuxiasumari

