2026-11-04  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	out_dxf: cquote: actually convert MIF \M+nXXXX to \U+XXXX
	cquote was meant to turn old Asian MIF codes \M+nXXXX into \U+XXXX
	(commit 0ad71990) but never did: it tested s[3] (the first hex digit)
	for the codepage index n instead of s[2], so only codes starting with
	1-5 could match -- and the 932/949/950/1361/936 double-byte codes start
	with 8-F. sscanf("M+%d") also read n together with the leading hex
	digits (\M+38141 -> 38141), taking the "Invalid MIF index" branch.

	Read n as one digit (s[2]), require four hex digits, and convert via
	dwg_codepage_uwc. Keep the MIF code unchanged when the codepage has no
	such character, instead of emitting \U+0000.

	* src/out_dxf.c (cquote): test s[2] for n and s[3..6] for the hex code;
	  sscanf("%4X") the code; keep the MIF code as-is when not in the
	  codepage.

	Fixes GH #1495.
	Reported-by: hjkim-fieldro

2026-11-04  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	out_dxf: escape U+0080+ and convert codepage strings on the cquote path
	Two related dwg2dxf string bugs in the caret-quoting path (strings that
	contain a line break, a C0 control byte, or a \M+ escape):

	1. r2000-r2004 TV strings stored in the source codepage were passed to
	   dxf_fixup_string unconverted; the quoting path ran bit_utf8_to_TU on
	   the raw codepage bytes, which parsed them as UTF-8 and dropped the
	   non-ASCII characters (GH #1496). Set dat->codepage from the header
	   for pre-R2007 input, and take the codepage->UTF-8 conversion whenever
	   the string needs cquote, not only for r2007+ targets.

	2. bit_embed_TU writes every code point < 0x100 as one raw byte. For
	   U+0080-U+00FF that is an invalid UTF-8 byte in an r2007+ DXF and a
	   lead byte in an r2000-r2004 Asian-codepage DXF (GH #1497). Add
	   dxf_embed_TU, which escapes U+0080 and up as \U+XXXX, and use it in
	   the quoting path (bit_embed_TU itself is left unchanged).

	* src/out_dxf.c (dxf_embed_TU, new): like bit_embed_TU but escapes
	  U+0080-U+00FF as \U+XXXX instead of a single raw byte.
	* src/out_dxf.c (dxf_fixup_string): use dxf_embed_TU in the quoting path.
	* src/out_dxf.c (VALUE_TV, VALUE_TV0): convert to UTF-8 when the string
	  needs cquote, not only for r2007+; forward-declare dxf_needs_cquote.
	* src/out_dxf.c (dwg_write_dxf): set dat->codepage from the header for
	  pre-R2007 input so the cquote path can convert codepage TV strings.

	Fixes GH #1496.
	Fixes GH #1497.
	Reported-by: hjkim-fieldro

2026-11-04  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	out_dxf: dxf_fixup_zero_handle: avoid handing out an in-use handle
	dwg_next_handle returns the last non-zero object handle + 1, which is not
	the highest handle when the objects are not sorted by handle. A handle-0
	object (the decode leaves a number of them at 0) then landed on an
	existing handle -- the GROUP took handle 2, the *Model_Space
	BLOCK_RECORD, and the DXF became unloadable (GH #1356).

	Compute the real highest handle over objects and object refs and start
	the fresh-handle sequence there.

	* src/out_dxf.c (dxf_fixup_zero_handle): start from the highest handle in
	  objects and object refs, not dwg_next_handle's last non-zero + 1.

