2026-11-04  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	decode: read Inventor ACIDBLOCKREFERENCE entities as INSERT
	Inventor drawings (R2007-R2018) place their sheet content with
	ACIDBLOCKREFERENCE entities (class AcIdBlockReference). LibreDWG read
	them as UNKNOWN_ENT and out_dxf skipped them, so dwg2dxf dropped the
	whole sheet (paper space kept only its VIEWPORTs, and the *I<n> blocks
	were left unreferenced).

	Their entity data is exactly an AcDbBlockReference (insertion point,
	scale, rotation, extrusion, has_attribs, block header handle), so
	decode it as an INSERT. Check the class name before is_entity so it
	works even when the class flags are unusable (is_zombie).

	* src/decode.c: read ACIDBLOCKREFERENCE as DWG_TYPE_INSERT via
	  dwg_decode_INSERT, before the UNKNOWN_ENT/UNKNOWN_OBJ fallback.

