2026-11-03  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	classes: dispatch an object only by a class of its own type
	The writers and dwg_free read a variable-type object (type >= 500) by the
	struct of its class, dwg_class[type - 500], chosen in classes.inc by the
	class's dxfname. Only the decoder allocates the object from that class.
	in_json allocates it by its JSON object name and took the type number as
	given; json_CLASSES also skips an entry missing a mandatory field, which
	moves every later class down one index and leaves the skipped entry's
	fields to the next one. in_dxf types an object by the class of its
	dxfname, but keeps the object's own enum type when no class has that
	name, which then indexes whichever class sits there. Nothing checked that
	the class names the object's type, so dwg_write_json read the object's
	struct as another one, e.g. a SCALE as a MATERIAL: reads past the smaller
	struct and through its fields as pointers. A dxfname key after the type
	did the same to dwg_encode and dwg_free, which find the class by
	obj->dxfname. The DXF writers' type functions already refuse an object of
	another fixedtype; dwg_print gets the same check.

	- classes.inc: every dispatch to a type's function first requires
	  obj->fixedtype to be that type. Otherwise the class is handled as an
	  unknown one (dwg_free frees by fixedtype, as for a class whose dxfname
	  differs). The decoder sets the type from the class just before, so it is
	  unaffected.
	- out_json, print, encode: the UNKNOWN_OBJ/UNKNOWN_ENT fallback goes by the
	  object's supertype, the layout of its struct, not by the class's
	  item_class_id. print also read one class past the array and took class 0
	  for no class.
	- out_geojson indexed the classes by fixedtype - 500 instead of type - 500;
	  its LWPOLYLINE and GEOPOSITIONMARKER cases now need that object type, and
	  an unknown class is no printed feature.
	- in_json: after all sections are read (CLASSES may follow OBJECTS), each
	  object stored with a class is typed by the class of its name, as
	  dwg_encode_get_class does for in_dxf, and that class gets the object's
	  supertype. A skipped CLASSES entry is cleared and the classes are
	  numbered by their index. A dxfname key after the type no longer replaces
	  the dxfname of the object's name (UNKNOWN_* keep theirs). A fixed type
	  number other than the object's own is replaced by the object's type, as
	  one up to LAYOUT, PROXY_ENTITY or PROXY_OBJECT already was (f23fcbb9):
	  dwg_free_object and the writers switch on it.

	add_test: JSON import with skipped classes, CLASSES after OBJECTS and a
	foreign dxfname types each object by its class; a SCALE whose only class
	is a MATERIAL is written as UNKNOWN_OBJ, and one of type 499 is typed as
	a SCALE.

