	indxf: keep group-9 LTYPE dash text in strings_area from DXF
	add_LTYPE_dashes stores the group-9 text dash into strings_area, but the
	LTYPE table-entry processing then re-allocated strings_area unconditionally
	(256 bytes for a <=r2004 source, 512 for >=r2007) after the read, discarding
	the text and leaking the old buffer. The LTYPE was then encoded with an
	empty strings_area, so a text dash lost its label on every DXF->DWG read.

	Guard both re-allocations with !_obj->strings_area so the buffer filled by
	add_LTYPE_dashes survives; LTYPEs without a text dash still get their
	allocation.

