	LTYPE "GAS" with a text dash (pattern A,.5,-.2,["GAS",STANDARD,...],-.25)
	previously roundtripped with an empty group 9; it now keeps "GAS" (TV 256
	for r2000, upconverted to TU 512 for r2013 by the #1486 upconvert).

	* src/in_dxf.c (LTYPE table-entry): Only allocate strings_area when it is
	  not already set by add_LTYPE_dashes.

2026-11-03  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	encode: upconvert LTYPE strings_area for DXF input to r2007+ targets
	add_LTYPE_dashes sizes strings_area by the source version during the DXF
	read (256/TV for a <=r2004 source). dxf2dwg restores header.version to
	the -a target (e.g. r2013) only after the read, so the r2007+ encoder
	then writes 512/TU bytes into the 256-byte buffer and overflows in
	bit_write_TF (via dwg_encode_LTYPE_private).

	The blanket INDXF early-return in dwg_convert_LTYPE_strings_area skipped
	the 256->512 upconvert for DXF input. The upconvert reads old[0..255] and
	writes new[i*2], safe on a 256-byte buffer, so allow it. Keep skipping
	the r2007->r2004 downconvert, which reads old[i*2] up to index 510 and
	would overread a 256-byte DXF buffer.

	Verified on a clang ASan build: dxf2dwg -y -a r2013 on an R2000 DXF with a
	text dash (group 74 bit 2 + group 9) previously crashed with
	heap-buffer-overflow in bit_write_TF (0 bytes after a 256-byte region
	from add_LTYPE_dashes); it now converts cleanly and the LTYPE roundtrips.

	* src/encode.c (dwg_convert_LTYPE_strings_area): Run the r2004->r2007
	  upconvert for DXF input; only the downconvert stays skipped.

