2026-11-03  Saddam  <saddamr3e@gmail.com>

	out_json: fix thumbnail overread in json_thumbnail_write
	json_thumbnail_write skipped a 16-byte sentinel whenever
	header.from_version >= R_2004 and then wrote thumbnail.size bytes.  Only
	the r2004+ DWG decoder keeps that sentinel in the buffer (thumbnail.byte
	= 16).  The DXF and JSON importers store the bare image with byte 0, so
	writing an r2004+ DXF or JSON as JSON read 16 bytes past the heap buffer
	into the output, e.g. the DXF of the in-tree example_2018.dwg.  Skip
	thumbnail.byte instead, as encode_r13_thumbnail and dxf_thumbnail_write
	already do.

	* src/out_json.c (json_thumbnail_write): offset the chain by
	  thumbnail.byte, not by from_version.

2026-11-01  Reini Urban  <rurban@cpan.org>

	out_dxf: do not split UTF-8 sequences in chunked strings
	dxf_write_chunked cut long (>250 byte) strings at a fixed byte offset,
	so a cut inside a multi-byte UTF-8 character left the following group
	5/3 chunk starting with a continuation byte and the first chunk ending
	in a truncated sequence. Strict DXF readers reject such files.

	For r2007+ (UTF-8 output), back off up to 3 bytes to the previous
	character boundary before the existing \U+XXXX backslash scan. Pre-r2007
	codepage output is unchanged.

	Verified with a 275 byte Cyrillic MTEXT (byte 250 is a continuation
	byte): master writes 2 invalid UTF-8 chunks, patched 0, and the
	concatenated chunks equal the original text.

	* src/out_dxf.c (dxf_write_chunked): Back off to a UTF-8 boundary.

	Fixes GH #1483
