2026-11-01  Reini Urban  <rurban@cpan.org>

	R11/R12: trailing entity bytes, block ATTRIB SEQEND, anonymous blocks
	Three fixes for pre-R13 (R11/R12) DWG files read via dwg2dxf.

	1. The entity size check rejected any entity whose declared size was
	   larger than what was parsed (e.g. DIMENSION, TEXT or ATTRIB with
	   trailing bytes), cut the size and read the next entity from the
	   wrong position, ending in a CRC error cascade. Tolerate up to 64
	   trailing bytes so the existing branch keeps them in unknown_rest.
	2. In the BLOCKS section only POLYLINEs got their trailing children
	   written, so an INSERT with ATTRIBs inside a block lost its SEQEND
	   and strict readers (ezdxf) rejected the file. Scan INSERT and
	   MINSERT too, and accept ATTRIB children.
	3. The R11/R12 block table stores anonymous blocks with a bare name
	   (*D, *U, *X), so many BLOCK definitions shared one name and every
	   DIMENSION resolved to the same one. Give them unique names, taking
	   the numbered name stored in the BLOCK entity when there is one, else
	   numbering after the highest used number, and keep BLOCK_HEADER and
	   BLOCK names in sync.

	Verified: a dxf2dwg --as r12 file with INSERT+ATTRIB in a block emits
	INSERT ATTRIB SEQEND on the patched build and no SEQEND on master;
	ACEL10/ACEB10 headers now carry the stored *X16/*X17/*D<n> names, bare
	*D in entities-2d/3d becomes *D1. The r10-r12 samples read unchanged.
	No available sample has trailing entity bytes, so part 1 is untested
	beyond the sample regressions.

	* src/decode.c (dwg_decode_add_object): Allow 64 trailing bytes.
	* src/out_dxf.c (dxf_block_write): Also scan after INSERT/MINSERT, accept
	ATTRIB children.
	* src/decode_r11.c (number_anonymous_blocks): New, called at the end of
	decode_preR13.

	Fixes GH #1481
