	dwgrewrite: keep the version for all files <= r2004
	The encoder can write r2004, so only downgrade 2007+ files, and to
	r2004 instead of r2000 (less lossy, keeps the 2004 section layout).

	This exposes two pre-existing r2004 write bugs in dwg_encode:

	* realloc-grown section_info entries were not zeroed, so the new
	  info->sections pointer held stale (poisoned) memory; freeing it
	  in the stream loop crashed with SEGV (example_2004, example_2010).
	  Zero the new entry after the realloc.

	* the read-time info->sections arrays were overwritten by the
	  pre-calculated ones without being freed: 193 byte leak in 13
	  objects for example_2004 (calloc in read_R2004_section_info).
	  Free them before the calloc, like the drop loop already does
	  for entries that are not written.

