2026-10-31  Reini Urban  <rurban@cpan.org>

	encode: restore TABLE_value data_type after kGeneral pre-clear
	The kGeneral (0x200) pre-clear in TABLE_value_fields rewrites the
	stored data_type when encoding to a pre-R2007 version (kGeneral is
	not representable there, it is written as kUnknown).  The rewrite
	persisted in the object, so the subsequent free dispatch switched on
	the corrupted value (0 = kUnknown) and never freed value.data_date,
	a 2 byte leak for every kGeneral value.  Reproducible with
	dwgrewrite example_2004.dwg (as r2000) under ASan: Direct leak of
	2 byte(s) in dwg_decode_TABLECONTENT_private.

	Save the data_type in encoder mode and restore it at the end of the
	macro, so the stored object keeps the decoded value as the source
	of truth for free/JSON/DXF.

	* src/dwg_spec_shared.h: wrap TABLE_value_fields in a scope with
	  save/restore of value.data_type around the kGeneral pre-clear.

