	dynapi: size the TABLE.cells count local like its dynapi field
	gen-dynapi.pl emitted a BITCODE_BL count local for every pointer
	field's count check, but TABLE.num_cells is an unsigned long
	(computed as num_rows * num_cols). dwg_dynapi_entity_value then
	wrote 8 bytes into the 4-byte local, corrupting the adjacent stack
	slot and aborting dynapi_test at the first TABLE object:
	"stack smashing detected" on the clang CI and abort trap on macOS,
	both before the first TAP line.

	Look up the count field's type in the dynapi table and size the
	local accordingly; only TABLE.num_cells is wider than BL today.

	 src/gen-dynapi.pl
	   Size the count-pair local from the count field's dynapi type.
	   (Also perltidy-normalized one adjacent line, as the hook
	   requires.)
	 test/unit-testing/dynapi_test.c
	   Regenerate: TABLE.cells count local is unsigned long.
