	bytes in the reproducer) was never freed since 6cb65e748, which
	disabled the free because "it's 0x21, not a pointer. Someone is
	overwriting it, because it's shared with TABLECONTENT" - the TABLE
	and TABLECONTENT objects alias the same struct memory. Re-enable the
	free, guarded: glibc aligns every allocation to 16 bytes, so only
	plausible heap pointers are freed and unaligned sentinel values such
	as 0x21 are left alone. The underlying aliasing remains a separate,
	open refactor ("use a subclass instead").

