	stored kGeneral (512) to kUnknown (0) before the switch on
	data_type. The kGeneral payload value.data_date was then neither
	emitted (corrupting the JSON/DXF output) nor freed (the 2-byte leak
	in the reproducer, TABLECONTENT object 467). Restrict the pre-clear
	to decoder/encoder modes, where it is a no-op at decode time (the
	field is still zero) and only affects pre-R2007 encode output.

	Verified: dwgread on the reproducer reports no leak anymore, and the
	JSON now carries value.data_type 512 / data_size / data_date instead
	of a corrupted kUnknown. make check (asan build): leak summaries
	91 -> 44 (all 42 occurrences of these two leaks gone, 0 SEGVs), and
	dwgfilter.test and svg.test now pass (6 -> 4 failing tests, same
	set otherwise).

