	attrib: fix R2010+ ATTRIB and R2018 multi-line ATTRIB/ATTDEF reading
	R2010+ ATTRIB objects do not carry the R2018 multi-line (mtext)
	subclass, so reading the keep_duplicate_records RC field as if present
	desyncs the decoder and leaves the ATTRIB misread. R2018 multi-line
	ATTRIB/ATTDEF (mtext_type > 1) additionally embed an AcDbMTextObject
	subclass - its own common data, the full MTEXT field set and a separate
	handle stream - that the decoder never consumed, so the main style
	handle was read from an embedded-MTEXT slot.

	This reworks the ATTRIB/ATTDEF decode to match the actual stream:

	* src/dwg.spec
	  - Drop the keep_duplicate_records RC field from ATTRIB (kept for
	    ATTDEF, DXF and JSON): the R2010+ ATTRIB stream does not carry it.
	  - Move the main style handle ahead of the R2018 mtext subclass in
	    both ATTRIB and ATTDEF so it is read at its true position in the
	    handle stream rather than grabbing an embedded-MTEXT handle.
	  - Encoder fallback: when writing below R2018 from an R2018+ file,
	    substitute text_value (ATTRIB) / default_value (ATTDEF) from the
	    embedded mtext.text so the downconverted text is not lost.

