	in_dxf: convert r2007+ UTF-8 strings to the pre-r2007 target codepage
	dxf2dwg --as r2000 of any r2007+ (AC1021+) DXF double-encoded every
	non-ASCII string: the UTF-8 bytes were stored raw in the codepage TV
	fields and re-decoded as cp125x on the way out ("CAÑERÍA Ø150" came
	back as "CAÃ‘ERÃ\x8dA Ã˜150"). The generic dynapi field path never
	converted from UTF-8 for TV targets.

	Convert in dxf_read_pair, only for the broken combination (source
	>= r2007, target < r2007, using the header codepage), with
	bit_utf8_to_TV; unrepresentable chars degrade to \U+XXXX as AutoCAD
	does. Converting at the reader gives the value the same encoding as
	one read from a pre-r2007 DXF, so every downstream consumer
	(generic dynapi fields, EED) behaves identically to the already
	working pre-r2007 path.

	The in_dxf call sites that pass pair values to dwg_add_u8_input now
	use dxf_pair_string(): for a pre-r2007 target the pair value is
	already in the target encoding (plain copy; feeding it through
	dwg_add_u8_input again would treat the codepage bytes as UTF-8 and
	mangle them), for a r2007+ target the UTF-8 value is converted as
	before.

	in_dxf.c:
		* dxf_read_pair: UTF-8 to TV conversion for a pre-r2007 target
		* dxf_pair_string: new, target-encoding aware copy for pair values

