2026-10-30  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	dec_macros: fix heap overflow in TRACE field-name logging
	FIELD_G_TRACE and the other FIELD_*_TRACE macros built the log field name
	with strrplc, which allocates a buffer sized only for the (possibly
	shortened) name, then strcat'ed a longer format suffix (": " FORMAT "
	[TYPE %d]") into it. For a repeated sub-field (a name containing
	"[rcount1]"/"[rcount2]", e.g. MLINESTYLE lines) with TRACE logging (-v3)
	this wrote past the buffer's end.

	Grow the buffer with realloc to fit the suffix before strcat'ing, and skip
	the log line if the realloc fails. Log-only path, gated on
	DWG_LOGLEVEL >= TRACE.

	Fixes a reproducible "malloc(): corrupted top size" crash in dwg2dxf on
	files with an MLINESTYLE when run with -v3, and an AddressSanitizer
	heap-buffer-overflow in dwg_decode_MLINESTYLE_private.

	* src/dec_macros.h (FIELD_G_TRACE, FIELD_G_TRACE_ANGLE, FIELD_TRACE,
	  FIELD_VEC_TRACE_N, FIELD_2PT_TRACE, FIELD_3PT_TRACE): realloc the
	  strrplc buffer to fit the appended suffix before strcat.

