	in_dxf: read ACAD_TABLE cells and TABLECONTENT from DXF
	Reimplement, independently from the PR description, the DXF reading of
	the TABLE entity cells and the TABLECONTENT object for PR #1446. The
	DWG reading of TABLE/TABLECONTENT/TABLESTYLE in normal builds was
	already done; this commit completes the DXF side so that dxf2dwg no
	longer aborts on files (example_*.dxf) that carry an ACAD_TABLE entity
	and a TABLECONTENT object.

	ACAD_TABLE is an entity that derives from INSERT; AutoCAD writes it to
	every DXF version in the pre-R2010 form. in_dxf now reads the repeated
	cell groups (171..178, 91, 145, 92, the 301 CELL_VALUE..304
	ACVALUE_END value block, and the per-cell border/grid data 302..309)
	via a dedicated add_AcDbTableCells handler, dispatched on the 171 code
	of an AcDbTable entity. The cell run is bounded only by the next
	subclass (100) or entity (0); the table-level override flags
	(table_flag_override 93, border_*_overrides 94/95/96) are read by the
	generic field loop before the cells, and 93/94/95/90 also occur inside
	each cell's value block and border data, so they must not terminate the
	cell run.

	TABLECONTENT is not imported from DXF (it is written as a placeholder,
	matching the PR). Its nested ldata/tdata/fdata fields are sub-fields of
	embedded structs, not top-level fields, so the generic field loop cannot
	match them. An unmatched code for an importable class is fatal, which
	made one unmodelled TABLECONTENT abort the whole file; the fallback now
	warns and skips past those codes instead.

	Also fix the TABLE title/header/data text style DXF code (AutoCAD
	writes 343, not 7), enable the TABLE and TABLECONTENT classes in normal
	builds, size strrplc dynamically, and add downconvert_TABLE for
	R2010+ -> R2000 writing.

	 src/classes.inc, src/objects.c, src/objects.in
	  Enable TABLE and TABLECONTENT in normal (non-DEBUG_CLASSES) builds.
	 src/dwg2.spec
	  Remove the #if defined (DEBUG_CLASSES) || defined (IS_FREE) guard
	  around the TABLE/TABLECONTENT/TABLESTYLE definitions. Read the 20.4.99
	  cell value unconditionally (kGeneral is a BL byte count + UTF-16LE
	  bytes, also present before R2007 in AutoCAD 2008 round-trip data).
	  Use unchecked REPEAT_C/REPEAT2_C for the cell vectors (cell text lives
	  in the string stream). Fix the text style DXF code 7 -> 343.
	 src/dwg_spec_shared.h
	  TABLE_value_fields: read kGeneral (512) for all versions as a BL byte
	  count plus UTF-16LE byte array, not only since R2007.
	 src/dynapi.c
	  Regenerate: TABLE title/header/data_text_style DXF code 7 -> 343.
	  (perl src/gen-dynapi.pl; no other changes.)
	 src/encode.c, src/encode.h
	  downconvert_TABLE: build the pre-R2010 table layout for R2010+ ->
	  R2000/R2004; declare it in encode.h.
	 src/common.c
	  strrplc: size the destination buffer from the actual replacement
	  length instead of a fixed 160 bytes (the -v3 nested table field-name
	  trace aborted on the old assert).
	 src/in_dxf.c
	  add_AcDbTableCells: read the ACAD_TABLE cell run. Dispatch on 171 for
	  an AcDbTable entity. Make the unmatched-code fallback non-fatal for
	  TABLECONTENT (warn and skip) so an unmodelled TABLECONTENT does not
	  abort the file.
	 programs/dxf.test.in, programs/dxfb.test.in
	  Exclude TABLE from the r13/r14 roundtrip expect count: TABLE is
	  unstable, so dwg2dxf logs "Add entity TABLE" but does not write it to
	  the DXF, making the roundtrip one entity short.

	Verified in a TCC build: make check passes (programs: alive, dwgfilter,
	dxf, dxfb, json, svg; examples; top level; unit-testing). dxf2dwg of
	example_2000..2018.dxf reads the ACAD_TABLE entity (num_rows/num_cols/
