	in_dxf: keep xref flags and path from DXF BLOCK when importing
	The r13+ DXF BLOCK entity carries the xref/overlay/resolved bits in
	code 70 and the xref path in code 1; the BLOCK_RECORD table entry has
	neither (its 70 is not emitted by writers). in_dxf ignored both, so an
	imported xref block came back as a regular block: 70 = 0 and an empty
	path.

	- src/in_dxf.c
	  * new_object: read BLOCK 70 (r13+) into the owning BLOCK_HEADER:
	    blkisxref (bit 4), xrefoverlaid (bit 8), xref_loaded (bit 32) and
	    flag |= bits 4/8, matching the DWG encode/decode layout.
	  * dxf_blocks_read: borrow the BLOCK entity's xref_pname (1) into the
	    BLOCK_HEADER when the block is actually an xref/overlay. Ordinary
	    blocks may carry their name in 1 (ODA convention), so the transfer
	    is limited to blkisxref/xrefoverlaid blocks; the pointer moves, the
	    BLOCK side is nulled so the header free owns it.

	Verified with a hand-made r2000 host DXF with an xref BLOCK (70 = 4,
	1 = ./FormatoA4.dxf): master roundtrips it as 70 = 0 and an empty
	path; with this patch the roundtrip keeps 70 = 4 and the path,
	likewise 70 = 12 (xref + overlay). Non-xref files (r11, r14, r2000,
	r2013 corpus DXFs) roundtrip byte-identical to master; add_test,
	dxf_test, bits_test, common_test, dynapi_test, hash_test pass.

