	bit_read_CMC read the colour index and then discarded it for every
	R2004+ CMC, re-deriving it from the rgb via dwg_find_color_index.
	Several ACI entries share one rgb (255 collides with palette 5,
	0x0000FF), so a stored colour 255 was emitted as 5. This is the same
	defect 9263d72d fixed in bit_downconvert_CMC, arriving through the
	read path. Keep the file's index when it is usable, and only fall back
	to the palette lookup when it is not.

	Also the LAYER DXF writer recovered a 256 index as rgb & 0xFF
	unconditionally. For true RGB colours (method 0xc2) the low byte is
	just the blue channel: a layer with rgb 0xC200A600 was exported as
	group 62 = 0, an illegal ByBlock layer colour. Gate the recovery on
	method 0xc3 (ACI), where the index really is packed in the low byte.

	* src/bits.c (bit_read_CMC): Guard the palette fixup like 9263d72d.
	* src/dwg.spec (LAYER): Only recover the index from the rgb for
	  method 0xc3.

	Fixes GH #1415

	Reported by hallelk, https://github.com/hallelk

2026-10-29  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

