2026-10-29  Joël Marth  <joel.marth@mytum.de>

	dxfb: don't let block bodies advance the BLOCK_HEADER scan (#1409)
	dxfb_blocks_write() walks dwg->object[] for BLOCK_HEADERs and passed its
	own loop index to dxfb_block_write(). Writing an INSERT with attributes or
	a POLYLINE inside that block advances the index by num_owned + 1, which is
	right for the ENTITIES walk but here skips the BLOCK_HEADERs that follow:
	their bodies are never written to the binary DXF, dwg2dxf -b still exits 0.
	Pass a copy.

	The ASCII writer dxf_blocks_write() has the same loop and was fixed in
	11d9a9bd9, this is the same fix for the binary DXF writer.

	* src/out_dxfb.c (dxfb_blocks_write): Pass a copy of the loop index to
	  dxfb_block_write().

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

