	spec: decode the r2010 AcDbAssocAnnotationActionBody layout
	Until r2010 (AC1024 included) the annotation action bodies start with the
	AcDbAssocActionBody and AcDbAssocParamBasedActionBody blocks. The spec
	guarded them with "if (actionbody)", a handle which is never set while
	decoding, so they were skipped and the following fields were read from the
	wrong bits. Only since r2013 a BS version and a dependency handle replace
	them.

	The r2010 sample proves that r2010 still uses the old layout: the BL
	class_version 1 read at the start of the object was the aab_version, and
	the 8 old fields end exactly at the class_version 0 and the two handles.

	Verified with example_{2000,2004,2007,2010}.dwg and example_r14.dwg
	(ASSOCALIGNEDDIMACTIONBODY): the object now consumes exactly its bits.
	example_2013.dwg (the r2013 layout) is unchanged and still leaves 2 bits.

