2026-10-28  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	decode: do the R2004 section page bounds checks in 64 bit
	read_2004_compressed_section added the page address, a copy size and
	max_decomp_size as uint32_t, so crafted values wrapped the sums and passed
	the checks. With address == the allocation size and a wrapped size of
	about 4GB the memcpy then started at the end of dec.chain and ran 4GB far.
	info->size - address wrapped the same way when address > info->size.

	* src/decode.c (read_2004_compressed_section): Add address and size or
	  max_decomp_size in uint64_t. The copy size is page_size when the page
	  address is beyond info->size, instead of a wrapped difference.

	Fixes GHSA-rhh7-9m95-rh87.

2026-10-28  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	decode: keep the R2004 section address 64bit
	read_2004_compressed_section stored the section map address (a 64bit
	Dwg_Section.address) in a uint32_t, truncating it, and then checked it
	against the input size. Keep it as uint64_t, and compare without any
	addition that could wrap: address > size || size - address < 32.

	* src/decode.c (read_2004_compressed_section): Use uint64_t for address,
	  mask with the low 32 bits only for the section header decryption, print
	  it with PRIu64.

	Follow-up to GHSA-6xx6-g44h-929j.

