2026-10-22  Damien  <114640315+Umbo-Damien@users.noreply.github.com>

	dxf: write LAYOUT 331 from viewports[0] when active_viewport is NULL
	The handle of the overall paperspace viewport (DXF group 331 of the
	LAYOUT object, the VIEWPORT with id 1) is the only reliable way for a
	DXF reader to tell the sheet's own view from the viewports onto the
	model. AutoCAD and the ODA converter always write it, taking the first
	entry of LAYOUT.viewports when active_viewport is NULL. We only wrote
	active_viewport, so for layouts saved with a NULL active_viewport (11
	of 41 layouts in a set of 36 AutoCAD 2013/2018 drawings) the DXF had
	no 331, and readers mistook the sheet view, at scale 1:1, for a
	viewport onto the model. The value itself was decoded correctly: the
	JSON output shows it as the first element of viewports.

	* src/dwg.spec (LAYOUT): In the DXF writer, when active_viewport is
	  NULL or has a zero handle and viewports is non-empty, emit
	  viewports[0] as group 331.

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

