2026-10-22  Saddam  <saddamr3e@gmail.com>

	acds: bound the ACIS BinaryFile scan index to dat->size
	The AcDs datastorage decoder scans the decompressed section buffer for
	the "ACIS BinaryFile" marker.  When a marker has no following
	End-of-ASM marker and sits in the last 20 bytes of the buffer, the
	next-offset advance (j + 20) runs past dat->size.  The loop condition
	then evaluates "dat->size - i", a size_t that underflows to a huge
	value, and memmem reads far past the decompressed buffer.

	* src/acds.spec: Stop the scan once i reaches dat->size.

