2026-10-22  Artem Arbatski  <busch.artem@gmail.com>

	dwg2dxf: don't skip BLOCK_HEADERs after writing a block
	dxf_blocks_write() passed its loop index to dxf_block_write(), which
	advances it to the index of the last written entity. If a block's
	entities are stored later in the object stream than following
	BLOCK_HEADERs (typical for dynamic blocks in r2013+ files), those
	BLOCK_HEADERs were skipped and their BLOCK/ENDBLK and entities were
	missing in the DXF. INSERTs referencing them then pointed to empty or
	undefined blocks.

	Observed with an AC1032 drawing: 16 of 449 blocks (e.g. dynamic blocks
	'Transformator', 'Gebäude', 'E-Spule') were not written. With this fix
	all blocks are written with their entities.

