	in_dxf: pre-r2004 viewports keep their on/off state
	Before r2004 a DWG keeps a VIEWPORT on or off in the VX_TABLE_RECORD that
	in_dxf creates for it, not in the entity. Its is_on was never set (the
	line was commented out), so every viewport of a DXF converted to r2000
	or earlier was off: ODA File Converter reads them back with status 0 and
	AutoCAD shows the layout's viewports empty.

	is_on now follows the DXF 68 status once the viewport has been read: 0
	off, anything else (including -1, on but off screen) on. Checked with
