	viewport whose 68 is 0 stays off.

2026-10-12  Marco Sumari Tellez  <ing.sumari@gmail.com>

	DIMENSION_ANG2LN: read and write the stream points in their order
	In the DWG stream of a 2-line angular dimension the arc point (DXF 16)
	comes first, as a 2RD, then the points 13, 14 and 15, and last the second
	line's end (DXF 10) as a 3BD (ODA spec). The spec read the 2RD into def_pt
	and the last 3BD into xline2end_pt, so 10 and 16 were swapped on every
	read and every write -- dwg2dxf's own round trip agreed with itself, but
	ODA and AutoCAD saw the arc point where the line's end should be. The
	pre-R13 branch above already treats xline2end_pt as the arc point (16).

	The DXF and JSON outputs keep their order. Checked with ODA File Converter:
	123 of 123 such dimensions in 40 real drawings now have ODA's points (none
	before), and a DWG written by dxf2dwg reads back in ODA with its points
	(swapped before).

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

2026-10-12  Marco Sumari Tellez  <ing.sumari@gmail.com>

	LWPOLYLINE: keep per-vertex widths through DXF import and export
	Three bugs lost the start/end widths of an LWPOLYLINE:

	- in_dxf flagged per-vertex widths with flag bit 4, which in the DWG is
	  "has const_width"; "has widths" is 32. The DWG writer then wrote a
	  const_width of 0 and no widths at all, so a polyline drawn with widths
	  came back with none. The 41 test checked the same wrong bit.
	- in_dxf allocated the widths only on the 40 of vertex 0. The DXF writer
	  omits 40/41 for a vertex with no width, so a polyline whose first
	  segment has no width made CHK_array abort the import. The first 40 now
	  allocates, as the first 42 does for bulges.
	- The DXF writer emitted the widths only when num_bulges == num_points,
	  a condition copied from the bulges test: a polyline with widths and no
	  bulges was written without widths.

	Checked with ODA File Converter: a DWG written by dxf2dwg with these
	polylines reads back with every width, and on real drawings the widths
	dwg2dxf now writes are the ones ODA reads (none before). Over 197 real
	drawings dwg2dxf gives the same entity counts, and 962 polylines in 44
	drawings get their widths back.

