2026-08-26  Marco Sumari Tellez  <ing.sumari@gmail.com>

	in_dxf: MTEXT spacing fields default when their group is omitted
	DXF omits the optional groups 72 (flow direction), 73 (line spacing
	style) and 44 (line spacing factor) when they hold their default --
	ezdxf and AutoCAD both do -- and the importer stored the missing group
	as 0. An MTEXT with the ordinary single line spacing therefore came
	back with linespace_factor 0.0, and every line of the paragraph draws
	on top of the first one; dwg2dxf then writes the explicit 0 back out,
	so the corruption round-trips.

	0 is not a valid value for any of the three fields (the factor's
	documented range is 0.25-4.0), so the defaults can never override a
	real value. Set them when the object completes, next to the existing
	_3DFACE default -- the same shape as the MINSERT column/row default
	of PR #1385.

	Reproducer (one entity):
	  python3 -c "import ezdxf; d = ezdxf.new('R2000'); \
	    d.modelspace().add_mtext('LINE ONE\\\\PLINE TWO', \
	    dxfattribs={'char_height': 1.0}); d.saveas('two-lines.dxf')"
	  dxf2dwg two-lines.dxf -y -o two-lines.dwg
	  dwg2dxf two-lines.dwg -y -o back.dxf
	  grep -A1 ' 44' back.dxf   # 0.0 before, 1.0 with this patch

2026-08-26  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	bits, encode: fix bit_copy_chain undersized realloc, use bit_chain_init_dat
	bit_copy_chain: bit_chain_alloc() only grows the chain by the fixed
	CHAIN_BLOCK (4096 bytes), not by the actually needed size. When the
	tmp_dat content being appended exceeds that, the following bounds
	check silently aborts the copy, dropping data. Use
	bit_chain_alloc_size(dat, size) to grow by exactly what is needed.

	dwg_encode_eed: use the existing bit_chain_init_dat() helper instead
	of manually calling bit_chain_init() and copying from_version/version/
	opts by hand; same semantics, less duplication.

