	gen-dynapi: keep first DXF group code per field to fix MTEXT rect size
	When a field is re-used in an Embedded Object or annotative context
	under a different group code, the generator was overwriting the
	canonical DXF mapping. For MTEXT this mapped rect_width to 40
	(instead of 41) and rect_height to 41 (instead of 46), silently
	clobbering text_height. The fix scopes first-wins protection to
	the Embedded Object marker, keeping the canonical mapping.

	Reported by @tuxiasumari, GH #1321.

2026-07-26  Reini Urban  <reini.rurban@gmail.com>
	    omp + DeepSeek V4 Pro /high  <deepseek@deepseek.com>

	bits: fix r2000 TV length and bit_write_DD mode selection
	Two encoder bugs that corrupted round-trip output for r2000 DWG:

	* bit_write_TV: the trailing NUL is only counted in the TV string length
	  for >= R_2004; pre-r2004 lengths must equal strlen. Writing the NUL
	  into r2000 shifted every object body by one byte per string.
	* bit_write_DD: the raw-byte alias cast took the address of a local
	  pointer variable instead of the double value's own storage, and the
	  comparison used LOW words instead of the HIGH words that bit_read_DD
	  keeps from the default. This made partial-mode DD writes use random
	  mode decisions, corrupting e.g. INSERT yscale values on round-trip.

	Reported by @tuxiasumari, GH #1319.

