2026-07-26  Reini Urban  <reini.rurban@gmail.com>
	    omp + DeepSeek V4 Pro  <deepseek@deepseek.com>

	in_dxf: fix crashes importing AutoCAD dynamic-block DXFs
	Four independent fixes for importing real AutoCAD 2018 DXF files
	containing dynamic blocks (EVALUATION_GRAPH, FIELD, BLOCKSTRETCHACTION).

	* add_EVAL_Node: reset the per-node 92-counter (j) when a new node
	  starts (group 91), so the second node's group-92 values are not
	  misread as edge-list entries. Map group 95 to nextid per dwg.spec
	  rather than overwriting edge_flags with a misleading '!= 32' warning.
	* add_EVAL_Edge: use (i+1), not num_edges, as the realloc count --
	  num_edges is 0 on the first edge, giving a 0-byte allocation and
	  a heap overflow on the edges[0] store.
	* add_AcDbBlockStretchAction: allocate hdls[i].indexes and
	  codes[i].indexes before writing to them (xcalloc of the parent
	  array left those pointers NULL, producing a SEGV). Fix the codes
	  loop bound which was copy-pasted from hdls[i].num_indexes.
