	    omp + DeepSeek V4 Pro  <deepseek@deepseek.com>

	in_dxf/dwg: handle & ownership fixes
	Five ownership/handle-semantics fixes so that conformant readers
	(AutoCAD/BricsCAD/ODA) accept our r2000 output without recovery
	errors or warnings:

	1. SORTENTSTABLE sort handles: pass NULL instead of the owning object
	   pointer to dwg_add_handleref, preventing duplicate handle
	   registration in object_map that caused 3000+ "Duplicate handle"
	   errors and downstream block-owner corruption.

	2. SORTENTSTABLE.block_owner: for empty tables with no explicit
	   code-330 owner, derive block_owner by walking the ownership chain
	   (ownerhandle -> DICTIONARY -> BLOCK_HEADER) instead of leaving it
	   unset, which misled conformant readers.

	3. Regular (non-space) block member entities: use entmode 0 (explicit
	   owner) instead of entmode 3, matching AutoCAD/ODA convention.
	   entmode 3 caused conformant readers to resolve the owner as
	   *Model_Space and warn "BlockBegin owner Id is invalid" on every
	   block member.

	4. BLOCK_RECORD flag 70 xref bit: clear blkisxref when there is no
	   genuine xref path (xref_pname is empty), preventing bound/local
	   blocks such as A$C... anonymous blocks from being rendered as
	   unresolved Xref placeholders.

	5. dwg_set_next_objhandle: check object_map for whether the candidate
	   next_hdl value is already in use, and only reuse it if free;
	   otherwise fall through to computing a fresh handle via the normal
	   handseed path, avoiding ambiguous handle collisions when table
	   records are added after the main DXF import pass.

	Reported by @tuxiasumari, GH #1320.

