	decode: fix OOB read in decode_R2004_header section page map (GHSA-c8cq-gr5h-7c6j)
	src/decode.c (decode_R2004_header): validate that the section-page-map
	address + 0x100 does not exceed dat->size before reading the map.

	In the backward-search path (triggered when section_map_address >
	dat->size), the loop scans backward in 0x20 steps for the magic
	0x41630e3b and leaves `start` the last-tested offset.  The code then
	unconditionally reads 0x100 bytes from &dat->chain[start] without
	checking that start + 0x100 <= dat->size.  For a small or truncated
	R2004 file the read lands past the end of the dat->chain buffer,
	producing a heap-buffer-overflow READ (CWE-125).

	The guard also covers the normal (non-search) path where
	section_map_address <= dat->size: a file whose section map header
	crosses the file boundary is now rejected with DWG_ERR_VALUEOUTOFBOUNDS
	instead of reading past the allocation.

	Fixes GHSA-c8cq-gr5h-7c6j. No CVE yet.
	Reported-by: yPin9 <ypp0x7@gmail.com>

