2026-07-21  Marco Sumari Tellez  <ing.sumari@gmail.com>
	    Claude Fable 5  <noreply@anthropic.com>

	in_dxf: rational HATCH spline read knots as weights (index overrun)
	A rational spline boundary edge stores num_knots knot values (DXF code 40)
	BEFORE the per-control-point weights (also code 40). The importer decided
	knot-vs-weight purely on `l >= 0 && is_rational`, so every knot after the
	first was routed to the weight branch: it overwrote control_points[0].weight,
	never advanced the knot index, and left `l` stuck at 0 so the knot-complete
	reset never fired. The control points then indexed from the wrong base and
	ran past num_control_points ("wrong l N control_points index"), aborting the
	whole DXF import (READ ERROR 0x800) -- e.g. Planos Constructivos, a spline
	with num_knots=18 / num_control_points=14.

	Track a knots_left counter (set at code 95, decremented per knot) and only
	treat code 40 as a weight once the knots are consumed. Planos now imports
	and round-trips clean through ODA; 254 unit tests green.

2026-07-21  Marco Sumari Tellez  <ing.sumari@gmail.com>
	    Claude Fable 5  <noreply@anthropic.com>

	in_dxf: HATCH.has_derived must OR every path flag, not just the last
	has_derived controls whether pixel_size is written/read. in_dxf set it with
	`o->has_derived = flag & 4` per path, so it ended up holding only the LAST
	path's derived bit. The decoder computes has_derived as the OR of every
	path flag's 0x4 bit. When an earlier path was derived but the last was not
	(e.g. flags [7, 24]), the encoder skipped pixel_size while the reader
	expected it -> the 64-bit gap corrupted num_seeds and the HATCH became
	unreadable. Accumulate with |=.

	HATCH: spline-edge fit points/tangents only when num_fitpts > 0
	For a spline boundary edge (R2010+), the decoder read num_fitpts and then
	ALWAYS read the two 2RD tangents. AutoCAD writes the fit points and the
	start/end tangents only when the spline was defined by fit points
	(num_fitpts > 0). Reading them unconditionally overran the object and made
	the decoder lose bit-sync right after the first spline edge -- it silently
	dropped every remaining edge and path of that hatch. dwg2dxf then emitted a
	DXF whose 91/93 counts disagreed with the data present, and dxf2dwg baked
	that inconsistency into an r2000 file that AutoCAD/BricsCAD/ODA reject
	("Object improperly read: <AcDbHatch>"). Guard the fit-point/tangent block
	with `if (num_fitpts)`. On Detalles Plaza Yanque a spline-bounded hatch now
	decodes all 3 paths / 6 edges instead of 2 / 3. 254 unit tests green.

2026-07-21  Marco Sumari Tellez  <ing.sumari@gmail.com>
	    Claude Fable 5  <noreply@anthropic.com>

	dxf: hex-encode binary TF chunks (group codes 310-319)
	* src/out_dxf.c: FIELD_TF with a binary chunk group code (310-319),
