	in_dxf: reset hdl_idx per HATCH path — associative hatches lost their pattern
	* src/in_dxf.c (add_HATCH): each boundary path carries its own 97
	  handle-count and 330 handle list, but hdl_idx was never reset when a
	  new 97 arrived. The 330s of every path after the first failed the
	  (hdl_idx + 1) < num_boundary_handles guard and were rejected
	  ("Unknown DXF code 330 for HATCH"), leaving num_boundary_handles set
	  with a NULL boundary_handles array. The encoder then emitted a short
	  handle stream ("Invalid boundary_handles size 1. Need min. 8 bits,
	  have 3"), corrupting the rest of the entity: on decode the hatch came
	  back with pattern_scale 0 and no definition lines.

	Minimized reproducer: an associative two-path hatch (ring of two arc
	edges, each path with one source boundary handle). Before: pattern
	ANSI31 scale 2.5 -> scale 0.0, 0 pattern lines. After: identical
	roundtrip. On the originating real-world plan, all 57 hatches now
	roundtrip with zero differences.

