2026-07-14  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	in_dxf: unquote ^J/^M back to LF/CR in DXF strings
	out_dxf's cquote() writes embedded control chars in text values as caret
	codes (LF -> ^J, CR -> ^M), and dxf_read_string already reverses cquote's
	\\M+nxxxx -> \\U+xxxx mapping, but not the caret codes. So a
	dwg->dxf->dwg roundtrip turned an embedded newline into the literal two
	bytes ^J: e.g. a TOLERANCE feature-control-frame text_value

	  {\\Fgdt;r}%%v1%%v2%%v%%v%%v\n10   (original)
	  {\\Fgdt;r}%%v1%%v2%%v%%v%%v^J10    (after roundtrip)

	Add the inverse ^J -> LF, ^M -> CR in dxf_read_string, next to the
	existing \\M+ handling, so text with embedded newlines round-trips.
	Verified on example_2007 TOLERANCE (text_value now identical after
	roundtrip); no over-conversion of other strings, ASAN clean.

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

