	in_dxf: use correct handle code for SEQEND-owned vertex/attribs
	dxf_postprocess_SEQEND rebuilt the owner's owned-child list
	(POLYLINE.vertex[] or INSERT.attribs[]) with handle relation code 3 for
	every child, but the encoder writes most of these as soft pointers
	(code 4):
	  - INSERT/MINSERT.attribs[]                HANDLE_VECTOR(..., 4)
	  - POLYLINE_PFACE/MESH.vertex[]            HANDLE_VECTOR(..., 4)
	  - POLYLINE_2D/3D.vertex[]                 HANDLE_VECTOR(..., 3)
	So on re-encode each PFACE/MESH vertex and each attrib warned
	'Expected a CODE 4 handle, got a 3'.

