2026-07-13  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	decode_r2007: bound page->offset (heap OOB read via size_t underflow)
	read_data_section set the source cursor from an unbounded page offset:
	  dat->byte = page->offset;
	page->offset accumulates unchecked page sizes in read_pages_map; only
	section_page->offset (the destination into decomp) was validated. In
	the uncompressed branch (comp_size == uncomp_size) the guard
	  section_page->uncomp_size > dat->size - dat->byte
	underflows when dat->byte (= page->offset) > dat->size, since both are
	size_t, so it wraps to ~2^64 and passes. The following memcpy then
	reads uncomp_size bytes from dat->chain + page->offset, past the file
	buffer -> heap out-of-bounds read (DoS, limited disclosure) on a
	crafted R2007 DWG.

	Reject page->offset >= dat->size before assigning dat->byte, which also
	makes the dat->size - dat->byte subtraction below well-defined and
	guards the compressed read_data_page path from the same bad cursor.

	GHSA-pcp5-hv9w-8f78. No behavior change for valid files (120 r2004/
	r2007 test DWGs still decode ASAN-clean).

	Reported-by: zx (Jace) @manus-use
	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

2026-07-13  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	decode: fix R2004 section-info integer overflow (heap OOB read)
	read_2004_section_info computed
	  max_decomp_size = info->num_sections * info->max_decomp_size;
	with both factors BITCODE_RL (uint32) into a uint32_t, so the product
	wraps mod 2^32. The 0x2f000000 guard then checked the wrapped (small)
	value and passed, while the second guard at :2059 uses a non-wrapping
	int64 product and admits info->size up to ~4.29e9. The buffer was
	allocated with the small wrapped size but sec_dat->size was stamped
	from info->size, so bit_search_sentinel later scanned gigabytes past a
	~1.5MB allocation -> heap out-of-bounds read (DoS, limited disclosure)
	on a crafted R2004 DWG.

	Compute the product in uint64_t and reject before truncating to the
	uint32_t. info->size is then bounded by max_decomp_size via the :2059
	check, so the sentinel scan stays inside the allocation.

	GHSA-2m5x-9p64-6m3f. No behavior change for valid files (120 r2004/
	r2007 test DWGs still decode ASAN-clean).

	Reported-by: zx (Jace) @manus-use
	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

