2026-07-13  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	dynapi: keep imported strings as UTF-8, don't convert to TU
	dynapi_set_helper converted every string field to UTF-16 (TU) whenever
	the (target) version was >= R_2007, ignoring import mode. But DXF/JSON
	imports (DWG_OPTS_IN) keep strings as UTF-8 in memory, as the readers
	assume via IS_FROM_TU_DWG (from_version >= R_2007 && !DWG_OPTS_IN).

	The result of this set/get asymmetry: importing an R2007+ DXF/JSON
	stored table names (layer, style, dimstyle, ltype, appid ...) as
	UTF-16, which the UTF-8 readers then truncated to the first character.
	So 'Tavolo 2' became 'T' in the written DWG, and every by-name lookup
	(dwg_find_tablehandle) failed -> a flood of 'Unknown HEADER.CLAYER',
	'Unknown LAYER.ltype', 'Unknown <entity>.layer', 'Unknown ...style',
	'eed[].handle for APPID...' and 'TODO resolve common handle name'
	warnings on dxf2dwg / json2dwg of R2007+ files.

	Pass an is_import flag (dwg->opts & DWG_OPTS_IN) to dynapi_set_helper
	and route imported strings through the UTF-8 (ascii) branch regardless
	of version. Non-import paths (binary decode, dwg_add API) are
	unchanged. Fixes the truncated names and all the resolve warnings;
	dwg->dxf->dwg and dwg->json->dwg round-trips preserve every table name
	across r2000..r2018.

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

