2026-07-13  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	3DSOLID/REGION: fix off-by-one dropping last SAT block in DXF
	dwg_convert_SAB_to_SAT1() splits the converted SAT v1 stream into
	<=4096-byte blocks. The final 'smaller rest' block is written at index
	i, but i is not incremented afterwards, so num_blocks = i is one too
	small and the last block is always dropped.

	For multi-block geometry (e.g. large 3DSOLID) this only loses the
	trailing End-of-ACIS-data terminator, which ODA tolerates. For a small
	single-block REGION the whole SAT fits in one <4096-byte block, so
	num_blocks becomes 0 and no ACIS/SAT data is emitted at all: the DXF
	gets the AcDbModelerGeometry subclass markers but an empty body, and
	ODA reports 'General modeling failure' on the AcDbRegion.

	Set num_blocks = i + 1 so the last block is kept (block_size[num_blocks]
	== 0 stays as the terminator). Fixes the two empty AcDbRegion(176) and
	AcDbRegion(37D) in test-data/example_2007.dwg.

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

