	decode: fix integer overflow in 3DSOLID block_size bounds check (GHSA-6v3v-3gmq-63v4)
	The check 'AVAIL_BITS(dat) > 8 * FIELD_VALUE(block_size[i])' has an
	unsigned 32-bit overflow: for block_size > 0x1FFFFFFF the multiplication
	wraps around and bypasses the bounds check, allowing a crafted DWG to
	drive heap corruption during decode that manifests as a double-free
	during dwg_free cleanup.

	Fix:
	- Cast to int64_t before multiplication
	- Add MAX_SIZE_TF (0xFFF0) upper bound, matching the encoder guard

