	Fix OOM/timeout from unbounded bit_chain_alloc loops in write functions
	Extend the while-to-if + early-return hardening from bit_write_RC
	to all other write functions that can loop unboundedly on a
	corrupted write position (set by dwg_encode seeking to a garbage
	section address):

	bit_write_B, bit_write_BB, bit_write_TF, bit_write_TFv,
	bit_copy_chain.

	All follow the same pattern: if the initial alloc (of 4KB via
	bit_chain_alloc or of the exact needed size via
	bit_chain_alloc_size) does not bring the buffer size past the write
	position, return early instead of looping forever or allocating
	terabytes.

