	Fix UBSan SIGILL in Ref_cmp function pointer cast and infinite alloc loop in bit_write_RC
	The OSS-Fuzz issues 528659158 and 527085540, testcases
	clusterfuzz-testcase-minimized-llvmfuzz-{4679250872172544,6588975733866496}.dwg
	crashed with two different issues:

	1. SIGILL in bsearch: Ref_cmp had a non-standard signature
	   (const Dwg_Object_Ref *, const Dwg_Object_Ref **) but was cast to
	   (int (*)(const void *, const void *)) when passed to bsearch and
	   bsearch_ex.  UBSan's __ubsan_handle_function_type_mismatch traps
	   this incompatible function pointer cast with ud1.  Fix by changing
	   Ref_cmp to the standard bsearch-compatible signature and doing the
	   casts internally.  Remove the now-unnecessary casts at the callers.

	2. Timeout in dwg_encode: the corrupted R_10 file has a garbage
	   tbl->address in a section header.  dwg_encode seeks dat->byte to
	   this huge position and then calls bit_write_RL, which hits the
	   while (dat->byte >= dat->size) loop in bit_write_RC.  The loop
	   keeps allocating 4KB pages (MAX_MEM_ALLOC is 1TB, so up to ~268M
	   iterations).  With ASAN's slow realloc this hangs for 60+ seconds.
	   Fix by changing while to if in bit_write_RC and adding a post-alloc
	   guard that returns early when the buffer is still too small.

		* src/dwg.c (Ref_cmp): Change signature to
		int (const void *, const void *), with internal casts.
		(ordered_ref_add): Remove function-pointer cast at bsearch_ex call.
		(ordered_ref_find): Remove function-pointer cast at bsearch call.
		* src/bits.c (bit_write_RC): Change while to if, add overflow
		guard with early return.

