2026-06-25  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	json: fix blank/garbled r2007+ unicode text on Windows (GH #655)
	On native 2-byte wchar_t platforms (HAVE_NATIVE_WCHAR2, e.g. Windows)
	the JSON UTF-16 output path went through wcquote() + fprintf("%ls").
	"%ls" converts the wide string to the C locale's narrow multibyte
	encoding via wcrtomb(), which under the default "C" locale truncates
	at the first non-ASCII character.  For r2007+ strings starting with a
	non-ASCII codepoint (Cyrillic, Korean, U+0192 ...) this emitted an
	empty "text_value", and for Western text it produced non-UTF-8 bytes.

	JSON must always be UTF-8 regardless of platform locale, so always use
	the manual UTF-16->UTF-8 emitter print_wcquote().  GH #655.

	* src/out_json.c (VALUE_TEXT_TU): always expand to print_wcquote.
	  (print_wcquote): compile unconditionally.
	  (wcquote): removed, no longer used.
	* NEWS: mention the fix.

	Reported-by: Gian Maria Gentilini <<gentilinigm@users.noreply.github.com>>
	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

