2026-06-15  Pascal Bourguignon  <pjb@informatimago.com>

	in_dxf: concatenate MTEXT text split across group codes 3 and 1
	MTEXT text longer than 250 characters is emitted in DXF as one or more
	250-char chunks under group code 3 followed by a final (<250) chunk under
	group code 1. The importer overwrote o->text on each code 3 (and only
	reallocated when the new chunk was longer), and let the final code 1 fall
	through to the generic field setter, which overwrote again. The result was
	a single surviving fragment — a 1497-char paragraph imported as one byte.

	Handle codes 3 and 1 together for MTEXT and append each chunk (a short
	MTEXT still has only the code 1, handled as the first chunk). On
	dwg2dxf | dxf2dwg of a real R2018 multiline MTEXT the full text and all
	\P paragraph breaks now survive; short single-chunk MTEXT is unchanged.

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

