2026-06-12  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	encode: Fix heap-buffer-overflow in encode_auxheader
	for cross-boundary version conversion

	When a fuzzed AC1013 (R13c3) file has an unusual header.num_sections=3
	(decode doesn't normalize this since from_version==version) and is
	re-encoded as R2004, dwg_sections_init's recompute condition only
	handled downgrades (from_version > R_2000 && version <= R_2000),
	leaving num_sections=3 and header.section[] sized for 5 entries.

	The SINCE(R_2004a) encode path unconditionally calls encode_auxheader,
	which writes header.section[SECTION_AUXHEADER_R2000] (index 5) - one
	element past the end of the array.

	Replace the one-directional check with a symmetric XOR
	((from_version > R_2000) != (version > R_2000)) so both upgrades and
	downgrades across the R_2000 boundary trigger the recompute.

