2026-06-12  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	Fix assertion failure in section_move_before for R13 encoding
	When decoding an AC1500 (R2000b) file with header.sections=6 and
	re-encoding as R13, two section_move_before calls occur during section
	reordering. The first legitimately grows *pnum 6->7 (THUMBNAIL). The
	second moves TEMPLATE, which is already within the counted range -
	a reorder, not an insert - but the old code still tried to grow *pnum
	7->8, tripping assert(*pnum + 1 <= SECTION_R13_SIZE).

	Detect when id is already within [0, *pnum) and reorder it in-place
	via memmove without touching *pnum, mirroring the analogous branch in
	section_move_top.

