	* add_HATCH: move CHK_segs in code 97 handler into the num_fitpts branch
	  only, fixing a false error when k=-1 from the end_tangent handler.

	* add_HATCH: skip xcalloc(0) for HATCH fitpts to avoid encoder error
	  When num_fitpts is 0, xcalloc(0, size) on glibc returns a non-NULL
	  pointer, triggering the encoder validation "Invalid ... fitpts 0, set
	  to 0" error.  Only allocate fitpts when num_fitpts > 0.

	* add_LTYPE_dashes: fix heap buffer overflow via group-code-9 strings
	  (CWE-122).  Remove static dash_i counter (Variant B: persisted across
	  LTYPE calls) and add bounds check before copying into the 256/512-byte
	  strings_area buffer (Variant A: up to 4096-byte strings).

	GH #1209

2026-06-01  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	bits: fix memory leak on realloc failure in iconv retry path
	On realloc failure, free(odest) was commented out, leaking the original
	iconv output buffer.  Uncomment it.

2026-06-01  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	bits: fix stale errno check and src advancement in iconv success path
	After the iconv flush call, the success check used errno==0, but errno
	is not reset by successful iconv calls. If a prior E2BIG retry left
	errno set, the success path was taken as failure, freeing the correctly
	converted buffer and falling back.

	Also, the fallback passed src (which iconv advanced past consumed input)
	instead of osrc (the original pointer saved before conversion).

	Fix: check nconv != (size_t)-1 instead of errno, and pass osrc to the
	fallback codepage conversion.

	Reported-by: code review

2026-06-01  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>
	    omp + opus 4.6  <noreply@anthropic.com>

	encode: Fix double-free in bit_chain_free in 3DSOLID/BODY/REGION
	In COMMON_ENTITY_HANDLE_DATA (enc_macros.h), path 1 copies hdl_dat to
	a local dat1, then redirects hdl_dat to dat2. When dat1 is freed, it
	NULLs dat1.chain but the original struct (wrapper's _hdl_dat) still
	holds the dangling pointer. The DWG_ENTITY wrapper then double-frees
	through the stale _hdl_dat.chain.

	Fix: NULL hdl_dat->chain right after copying to dat1, so dat1 owns
	the buffer exclusively and the original struct can't be double-freed.

	Same class as CVE-2021-36080 (fixed in 9b6e0ff9 for MTEXT), but this
	3DSOLID/BODY/REGION instance was missed.

	Reported-by: Adam Taguirov <adam@sigreturn.com>

	* src/enc_macros.h (COMMON_ENTITY_HANDLE_DATA): NULL hdl_dat->chain
	after copying to dat1, before redirecting hdl_dat to dat2.

2026-06-01  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>
