	bits: Fix heap OOB read in bit_TV_to_utf8 (iconv path)
	Uncomment the NUL termination (*dest = '\0') in the iconv success path
	of bit_TV_to_utf8(). When iconv fills the destination buffer exactly,
	dest points one past the allocation and no NUL remains within bounds.
	The following bit_u_expand()/strlen() then reads past the heap chunk
	(CWE-125 OOB read / CWE-200 heap disclosure).

	Also extend all calloc/realloc sizes by +1 to always leave room for
	the terminator, even on the exact-fill and retry paths.

	Reported-by: Adam Taguirov <adam@sigreturn.com>

	* src/bits.c (bit_TV_to_utf8): Uncomment *dest = '\0' at the iconv
	  success path. Extend calloc and realloc by +1 for the NUL terminator
	  on the CP_UTF8 path, the iconv initial alloc, and the iconv retry
	  realloc.
	  Also in the iconv E2BIG retry path, fix two bugs:
	  1. destlen tracks remaining space; when iconv fills the buffer,
	  destlen=0, so destlen*=2 stays 0, then dest_new[destlen-1] writes
	  at dest_new[SIZE_MAX] (heap OOB-write underflow). Double odestlen
	  instead and compute the new destlen from it.
	  2. After realloc, dest was reset to dest_new (base), losing its
	  position within the buffer. The next iconv call would overwrite
	  previously converted output instead of appending. Preserve the
	  offset: dest = dest_new + (dest_old - odest_old).

	  Also remove the now-unnecessary dest_new[destlen-1]='\0' hack since
	  the NUL terminator is written at the success path
	  and the extra +1 in the allocation always leaves room.
	* test/unit-testing/bits_test.c: iconv NUL-termination test for
	  bit_TV_to_utf8 (commit dc8e3509).
	* test/unit-testing/encode_test.c: double-free test for
	  COMMON_ENTITY_HANDLE_DATA (commit 6deac10e).

	GH #1209

