2026-05-31  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	tests: fix decompress_R2004_section test vectors (wrong dec.size)
	The two decompress_R2004_section test cases used dec.size equal to the
	expected output length (123 and 53 bytes).  The real decoder allocates
	dec at max_decomp_size (0x7400 = 29696) per section.  With the smaller
	buffers the decompressor hit the end-of-buffer guard added to cap the
	large LZ77 back-copy that fills the page:

	  auxh: >C 29564 at dec[116] -> end=29680; 29680 >= 123 -> VALUEOUTOFBOUNDS
	  ofs:  iteration 4 end=55 >= 53, and later >C 30137 -> end=30192

	Fix: allocate 29696 for auxh (exact real-decoder size) and 32768 for ofs
	(covers the >C 30137 copy landing at dec[30192] plus 13 literals = 30205).
	The meaningful bytes in dec.chain[0..N-1] are identical; only the
	memcmp range is kept at sizeof(expected).

	* test/unit-testing/decode_test.c (decompress_R2004_section_tests):
	  Change dec allocation from sizeof(expected) to 29696/32768.  Remove
	  the now-wrong dec.size == sizeof(expected) check from the auxh test.
	  Restore fail() from todo().

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

