	Fix r11 dwgadd test: pre-R13 handle size mismatch for code 1

	In encode_preR13_entities, VALUE_HANDLE used handleref.size to decide
	whether to write an RC (1 byte) or RS (2 byte) handle.  For API-created
	objects dwg_add_handleref forces handleref.size to 2 for all pre-R13
	handles, but the decoder uses the handle_code argument (code==1 => RC,
	else RS) to decide the size.

	This caused a 1-byte misalignment for SHAPE entities, which use a
	code-1 style handle in r11 (and older).  The misaligned decoder then
	read garbage types and entered an infinite loop.

	Fix by using handle_code to pick the size, matching the decoder.

	src/enc_macros.h (VALUE_HANDLE): For pre-R13, ignore handleref.size
	and use handle_code == 1 ? 1 : 2.

	Co-Authored-by: Kimi-k2.6 <kimi@moonshot.cn>

