	For R13+ DWG files the VIEWPORT entity does not store the id (DXF 69)
	and on_off (DXF 68) fields in its binary format; they are only
	computed during DXF export.  This caused the API to report id=0 for
	all viewports after reading a DWG.

	Add a post-processing step in dwg_read_file that iterates over all
	objects and assigns auto-incremented viewport ids (starting at 1) to
	active viewports, and id=0/on_off=0 to the overall paperspace
	viewport (entmode 0).

	src/dwg.c (dwg_fixup_viewport_ids, dwg_read_file): New helper and call.

	Co-Authored-by: Kimi-k2.6 <kimi@moonshot.cn>

