2026-04-28  mmgehlot  <gehlot.21@gmail.com>

	test/bits: add aliasing-return regression for bit_TV_to_utf8
	Lock in the contract that bit_TV_to_utf8 may return its input `src`
	pointer unchanged on the fast paths exercised by VALUE_TV in
	out_dxf.c. Without explicit pointer-equality assertions, a future
	contributor could "tighten" the function to never alias and re-add
	ATTRIBUTE_MALLOC, silently re-introducing the optimizer-induced
	free() of caller stack buffers that this PR fixes.

	Asserts pointer equality on three paths reachable from the public
	function:

	  1. CP_UTF8 + pure-ASCII input without \U+/\M+ markers — the path
	     actually triggered in dxf_CMC for the Panchvati R2018 DWG that
	     surfaced the bug. Aliases on every build.
	  2. CP_UTF8 + empty string — same line-3372 branch as (1); aliases
	     on every build regardless of HAVE_ICONV.
	  3. CP_UNDEFINED — typically aliases via the `!charset`
	     short-circuit. On builds without iconv this routes through
	     bit_TV_to_utf8_codepage and may return a fresh allocation; both
	     are accepted (the contract is "alias OR fresh malloc", what's
	     forbidden is an attribute-malloc claim that lets the optimizer
	     elide the alias guard).

	Addresses qodo-code-review's PR #1250 finding "No regression test
	for aliasing" (PR Compliance ID 5: add tests for bug fixes).

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

2026-04-28  mmgehlot  <gehlot.21@gmail.com>

	bits: drop ATTRIBUTE_MALLOC from bit_TV_to_utf8
	bit_TV_to_utf8 is documented to "return ... the unchanged src string,
	or a copy" and in fact returns the input pointer on at least four
	paths:

	  - bit_TV_to_utf8_codepage: codepage == 0 fallback
	  - bit_TV_to_utf8: CP_UTF8 with no \U+/\M+ markers
	  - bit_TV_to_utf8: HAVE_ICONV + iconv() EINVAL fallback (returns
	    bit_u_expand(osrc), and bit_u_expand returns its input pointer
	    unchanged in pointer value)
	  - bit_TV_to_utf8: empty srclen via charset short-circuit

	Despite that, the prototype/definition were annotated
	__attribute__((malloc)). That attribute promises every non-NULL
	return is fresh, non-aliasing memory — which is false here.

	Under -O2/-O3, GCC and Clang exploit the malloc attribute to prove
	the alias guard in the VALUE_TV macro is dead code:

	    char *u8 = bit_TV_to_utf8 ((char *)value, dat->codepage);
	    dxf_fixup_string (dat, u8 ? u8 : (char *)value, 1, dxf);
	    if (u8 && u8 != (char *)value)   <-- compiler proves "always true"
	      free (u8);                     <-- becomes unconditional

	The guard is elided and free() is called on the caller's input
	pointer. In dxf_CMC (out_dxf.c:1261) the input is `char name[256]`
	on the stack, producing:

	  free(): invalid pointer  (SIGABRT, exit 134)

	Reproduced on a real-world Panchvati DWG (R2018) at -O2. AddressSanitizer
	confirms:

	  ERROR: AddressSanitizer: attempting free on address which was not
	  malloc()-ed: 0x7ff7b8b20e20
	    #1 dxf_CMC out_dxf.c:1261
	  This frame has 1 object(s):
	      [32, 288) 'name' (line 1234) <== bad-free target
	  SUMMARY: bad-free out_dxf.c:1261 in dxf_CMC

	The bug only manifests at -O2/-O3 because -O0/-O1 do not exploit
	the attribute hint, which is why test suites and debug builds
	miss it.

	Fix: remove ATTRIBUTE_MALLOC from both the prototype (src/bits.h)
	and the definition (src/bits.c) of bit_TV_to_utf8. The function's
	existing semantics (input-aliased return value is legitimate, and
	the VALUE_TV alias guard is correct) are preserved; we just stop
	lying to the optimizer.

	A separate audit of bit_TV_to_utf8_codepage shows it has the same
	issue (also annotated ATTRIBUTE_MALLOC, also returns (char *)src on
	codepage==0). It is static and only reached via bit_TV_to_utf8
	fallbacks; the alias guard at every reachable call site is the same
	VALUE_TV macro, so it is covered by this fix in practice. A
	follow-up may want to drop the attribute there too for defensiveness.

	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

