	The summaryinfo_address in the DWG file header was written as 0
	because it's set after sections are written but the header is
	written earlier. Add a patchup at 0x20 similar to thumbnail_address.

	encode: fix r2004 file_header for DXF import
	The R2004_Header file_dat was initialized with R_INVALID versions,
	so SINCE(R_2004a) in r2004_file_header.spec was skipped and
	header_size stayed 0, causing ODA "Out of range" errors.
	Copy version/from_version/opts from dat into file_dat.
	Also use IF_ENCODE_FROM_EARLIER_OR_DXF in the spec so header fields
	are initialized for same-version DXF imports.

	encode: skip obj_string_stream when bitsize is not yet known
	During encode, obj->bitsize is 0 (calculated after encoding).
	obj_string_stream computes start = obj->bitsize - 1 = 0xFFFFFFFF,
	causing bit_set_position buffer overflow errors for every r2007+ object.
	Guard both entity and object encode paths.

	encode: fix fixup_NOD is_tu check for DXF import
	Use IS_FROM_TU_DWG() instead of version >= R_2007, which accounts
	for the DWG_OPTS_IN flag. When importing from DXF, strings are UTF-8
	not TU, even when the target version is R_2007+.
	Fixes heap-buffer-overflow in bit_convert_TU.
	Also allow r2010+ encoding, and update WE_CAN message.

	improve/update fuzzing

	dwgfuzz: show mode with --version

	more fuzzing compilation fixes

	fix fuzzing, esp. the LOG macros must be statements now
	and yes, fuzzing only works with the 2 modern compilers.

	decode: fix fuzzer overflow case in xdata
	with wrong xdata_size overflowing also dat->size

	decode: fix fuzzer overflow in dwg_decode_add_object
	Fixes CIFuzz

