2026-03-28  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	dxfb: fix pre-R14 binary DXF group codes and roundtrip
	Fix GROUP macro in out_dxfb.c: use 0xFF escape prefix for codes >= 255,
	not >= 1000. Codes 255-999 (280, 281, 330, etc.) were silently truncated
	to their low byte, corrupting pre-R14 binary DXF output.

	Fix in_dxf.c reader to handle 1-byte group codes for pre-R14 binary DXF,
	with 0xFF escape for codes >= 255. Auto-detect the format by checking
	byte 23 after the sentinel.

	Also fix HEADER_RL to use VALUE_INT to respect DXF code sizes.

	Surprisingly fixes the last failing dxfb.test failure with example_2007
	roundtrips.

