2026-03-23  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	get_next_owned_entity: stop before skipping last_entity if it's a sub-entity type
	When last_entity is an ATTDEF (e.g. block "BLOKO" in example_r14.dwg),
	the while loop that skips sub-entity types (ATTDEF, ATTRIB, VERTEX...)
	advanced past last_entity before checking it, because the existing
	early-exit check was placed after the advance. This caused the
	traversal to continue beyond the block's boundary, emitting entities
	from subsequent blocks (duplicate SVG IDs, extra entities).

	Add an early-exit check before the advance inside the while loop so
	that if last_entity itself is a sub-entity type, it is returned
	immediately without skipping it.

	Reproducer: dwg2SVG example_r14.dwg produced duplicate dwg-object IDs
	due to block traversal running into the next block's entities.

	Fixes GH #1114

