2026-03-22  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	encode r11: always update entities_end after encoding
	The encoder only set entities_end when it was zero (from the input
	file). Since the input usually has a valid entities_end, the encoder
	kept the stale value instead of computing the new one from the output.
	This caused the second decode pass to read too few entities bytes,
	then interpret the BLOCK sentinel as garbage entity data, producing
	cascading errors like 'Invalid obj->size 53196 changed to 56'.

	Remove the 'if (!dwg->header.entities_end)' guard so entities_end is
	always set to dat->byte after encoding entities.

