2026-03-18  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	encode: fix bit_write_MS for overlarge values where value & 0xFFFF < 0x8000
	For overlarge MS values (> 0x7fff) where the lower 16 bits don't naturally
	have bit 15 set (e.g. 88177 = 0x15831), the first RS word was written without
	the required bit-15 flag. The reader uses bit 15 of the first word to decide
	whether to read a second word; without it, the size was decoded incorrectly.

	Values like 45924 (0xB364) happened to work because their lower 16 bits
	already had bit 15 set, masking this bug. Values like 88177 (0x5831 lower 16)
	caused wrong object sizes and cascading CRC failures on DXF roundtrip.

