2026-03-17  Reini Urban  <reini.urban@gmail.com>

	encode: fix CRC start address for overlarge MS objects. Fixes GH #1222
	When obj->size crosses the 0x7fff boundary (overlarge MS needing 2 RS
	words instead of 1), the memmove shifts data right by 2 bytes and
	obj->address is correctly adjusted. But `address += 2` wrongly shifted
	the CRC start address into the middle of the MS size field, so the
	written CRC covered only bytes 2..N instead of 0..N of the object.

	Also the size was not big enough.

	The decode side always passes the pre-MS object start to bit_check_CRC,
	so remove `address += 2` (overlarge) and `address -= 2` (downsize) to
	keep `address` at the true object start for bit_write_CRC.

